{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show a518cbb:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.interaction.review.md'","aggregated_output":"<!-- Reviewer: Codex gpt-6.2-astra, effort xhigh (observed in the session rollout, thread 01a1ecf0-d296-74e2-9845-a522366f5003), read-only, cross-provider. Reviewed commit 4809516. -->\n\n**Release verdict for `4809516`: blocked.** An assistive range adjustment can hang the page on scatter. Opening the table with a right-hand legend can cover the only control that closes it. The focused range also changes its accessible value text on ordinary appends. Whether each change is spoken remains unverified.\n\n## 1. Verification of the 22 earlier findings\n\nLine numbers refer to `4809516`. **Ran** means I exercised the named Node path. **Reasoned** means I traced the implementation or test. Severity in this table is the severity of the original finding. I limited controller inspection to the earlier findings that depend on it.\n\n| # | Severity and disposition | Sequence, evidence, criterion and remaining fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **B · Fixed. Reasoned.** | Pause, append A, replace with B, append C, zoom, resume. A successful replacement clears the held frame after validation. A rejected replacement leaves it intact. A paused append validates before committing and Resume consumes the latest held frame. This fixes the reported replay and strict-rejection sequences. **I6, plan 1.5.** [controller.ts:508](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:508) [controller.ts:549](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:549) |\n| 2 | **B · Partly fixed. Reasoned.** | With `A,B,C → B,C,D`, focused B remaps to B and focused A remaps to B as intended. The same successor rule is applied to a **pin** and to the target dismissed with Escape. Pin A and evict it and the pin silently identifies B. Dismiss A and eviction can suppress B without the reader ever dismissing B. Use successor resolution for keyboard focus and exact category identity for pins and dismissal. **A3, A7, I1, `DatumRef`.** [interaction.ts:1189](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1189) [interaction.ts:1244](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1244) |\n| 3 | **B · Partly fixed. Ran state inputs, reasoned through controls.** | A genuinely empty zoom retains the proxy, `-`, `0`, Shift+arrows, Zoom out and Reset. Resume is independent of `ready`. But an all-zero donut with `table:false` produced two slices, `ready=false`, `inspectable=false`. Its enabled legend disappears because inspectability is derived from the optional table. Derive slice-list availability from the slices. The recovery predicate also misidentifies loading and error states, detailed below. **I3, I6, F8, L7.** [interaction.ts:512](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:512) [interaction.ts:1091](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1091) [controller.ts:931](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:931) |\n| 4 | **B · Fixed for range correctness. Ran text generation, reasoned through DOM writes.** | Focus the first point and append three times. The generated texts ended in `Point 1 of 1`, `1 of 2`, `1 of 3`, `1 of 4`. Commit compares and updates native `max`, `value` and `aria-valuetext` independently. New points are reachable at the range boundary. A7 speech behavior remains open, as detailed below. **A3, A7, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:420](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:420) |\n| 5 | **M · Fixed with a new revision-lifetime defect. Reasoned.** | Normal draws retire superseded revisions. Paused appends retain a frozen frame and the newest store state. There is a boundary case on an established stream. Draw A, append B with `keep:1`, pause, append C before the next draw, then select still-visible A. The code freezes **accepted B**, retires A’s row source, and consults the frozen map only for B. A’s selection can therefore lose its caller row. Preserve the frame actually on screen until the atomic switch. This is the outstanding part of the original row-lifetime requirement. **I6, plan 1.5.** [controller.ts:551](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:551) [controller.ts:1170](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1170) [store-rows.ts:292](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-rows.ts:292) |\n| 6 | **M · Fixed with a new blocker. Ran the scatter steps, reasoned through the event loop.** | Home at the first point leaves no stale intent. Both `input` and `change` reconcile an aligned absolute value, and focus takeover now reads the pointer target first. In narrowed scatter mode, an absolute adjustment to an ordinal belonging to another series can loop forever. Resolve the requested ordinal in the global range order. **A2, A3, decision 0001, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:498](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:498) [interaction.ts:568](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:568) |\n| 7 | **M · Partly fixed. Ran.** | A hidden-only x is reachable, ordinary stacked totals are present, and Right stays in the chosen scatter series. With ten coincident points, the pointer returned eight refs and count ten. Focusing the earliest row failed the membership check and produced one ref and count one. With ten stacked series and one gap, the spoken text contained `incomplete` **three times**. Preserve the full coincidence count even when the focused ref falls outside the eight displayed rows. Format overflow series without adding the stack qualification to each one. **I1, A2, A3, §3.6.** [interaction.ts:316](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:316) [focus.ts:137](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:137) |\n| 8 | **M · Partly fixed. Reasoned.** | A tap emits `select`, and a mouse can select a secondary floating row. Click-centered zoom still cannot reproduce fixed-width pan. On the review’s sparse `[0,100]` chart, Shift+Right takes the empty `[25,75]` window to `[30,80]`. There is no datum to click in that window, and Zoom out or Reset returns to full width. A touch tap also never assigns `focus`, which is the anchor the zoom buttons read. Provide single-pointer pan or range-endpoint controls and retain the touch-selected anchor. **I3, I4, WCAG 2.5.1 and 2.5.7.** [interaction.ts:623](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:623) [interaction.ts:860](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:860) [interaction.ts:1062](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1062) |\n| 9 | **M · Partly fixed. Ran.** | Exhausted buttons expose `aria-disabled` and an ineffective full-view wheel operation passes through. But two and three aligned positions over `[0,100]` still produce minima of 200 and 100. Scatter over `[10¹⁶,10¹⁶+4]` produces a minimum of about 142, disabling even a representable halving. Category line, area and bar all returned `zoomApplies=false`. Use an attainable, direction-preserving minimum and implement ordinal zoom for line and area. I read §3.6’s unqualified “Yes” for those two types as including categories. I3 explicitly requires the continuous cases. **I3, I4, §3.6.** [focus.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:285) [focus.ts:310](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:310) |\n| 10 | **M · Partly fixed. Ran horizontal arithmetic, reasoned through cancellation.** | On a horizontal `[0,100]` projection the upper-quarter anchor was 75. Halving gave `[37.5,87.5]` and kept 75 under the fingers. The sign correction is sound. Escape consumes a captured mouse drag and a remaining pinch finger is suppressed as a tap. A cancelled pinch can still apply its queued animation frame, and the implementation can substitute a third finger into an existing pinch. Cancel pending work and bind the gesture to its original pair. **I3, I4.** [interaction.ts:836](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:836) [interaction.ts:913](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:913) |\n| 11 | **M · Partly fixed. Ran lookup cases, reasoned through pin presentation.** | Zooming a pinned scatter point outside x or hiding its series removes its visible ordinal. But changing y-domain to `[0,10]` for a pinned `(5,100)` left ordinal `1`, anchor `null`, and one formattable row. The pin survives at a fabricated center anchor. Appending eight duplicates to a pinned point likewise yielded a fresh pick of count nine while the fallback retained the original count one. Require a drawn anchor for a graphical scatter pin and rebuild its group from that position. **I1, A7, `PickTarget`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:377](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:377) [interaction.ts:1212](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1212) |\n| 12 | **M · Partly fixed. Reasoned.** | Floating candidates now respect ordinary clipping ancestors and fall back when none fits. Document scroll capture repositions pinned and keyboard tips. Under `scale(2)`, local deltas and translation still mix viewport and layout pixels, and tooltip size comes from untransformed `offsetWidth/Height`. The fallback readout itself receives no clipping-bounds check. Convert both picking and placement through one coordinate system and bound the fallback. Scroll handling addresses part of the report. Transforms and a clipped fallback still violate **I1, A2, A6**. [interaction.ts:671](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:671) [interaction.ts:945](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:945) [tooltip.ts:150](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:150) |\n| 13 | **M · Partly fixed. Reasoned.** | The readout survives the approach across the bottom axis, and moving the keyboard away and back clears dismissal. In the narrow tile the opaque readout still covers the controls. A touch pin applies `pointer-events:none`, so tapping a displayed row can activate an unseen button underneath. A mouse readout intercepts the controls instead. Reserve space for a reachable readout with independently visible controls. **I1, I4, A2, WCAG 1.4.13.** [interaction.ts:683](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:683) [tooltip.ts:196](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:196) [css.ts:150](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:150) |\n| 14 | **M · Fixed. Reasoned.** | Tab onto a donut whose first slice is zero. The plot ring is inset inside the clipped rectangle and `markLegend` outlines that slice’s list item even without an arc. This resolves the reported invisible-focus case. **F8, A2, WCAG 2.4.7.** [interaction.ts:398](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:398) [css.ts:190](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:190) |\n| 15 | **M · Partly fixed, with a new blocker. Reasoned.** | Opening a bottom-toolbar table overlays the current plot body. Now shrink the card or increase text size. The body retains its original inline pixel height and `flex:none`, so the pager or toolbar can fall outside the card. With a right-hand legend the overlay covers the disclosure itself. Keep the body responsive and confine the overlay to the plot column. **A4, A6, WCAG 1.4.10 and 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:998](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:998) [css.ts:235](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:235) |\n| 16 | **M · Fixed for the reported unsolicited page-count update. Reasoned.** | Leave page one open and append row 201. `render(false)` sets the status to `aria-live=\"off\"` before changing the page count. Reader paging uses `render(true)`. Actual speech, including reliable announcement when politeness is re-enabled, still needs rehearsal. **A7, WCAG 4.1.3.** [table.ts:140](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:140) |\n| 17 | **M · Fixed for the three original ordinary transitions. Reasoned.** | Reordering B restores the focused button. Removing an open table hands focus to its disclosure or the surviving proxy. Shrinking to one page moves focus from the pager to the scroll region before hiding it. The handoff still fails when the destination proxy is itself hidden or removed, detailed below. **A2, A4, WCAG 2.4.3.** [toolbar.ts:150](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/toolbar.ts:150) [table.ts:129](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:129) [interaction.ts:1018](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1018) |\n| 18 | **M · Partly fixed. Ran formatting, reasoned through submission.** | English `200,000` and the tested English date work, and parsing now reads the current x kind. The French table produced `1 234,5 ms`, which the numeric regex rejects. English `1,,2` becomes `12`. The wall-time fallback drops the time, category input is trimmed, and invalid submission still gives only `aria-invalid`. Match displayed values or parse by actual locale, unit and kind. Preserve exact categories and supply a visible associated error and example. **A4, A6, WCAG 3.3.1 and 3.3.2.** [interaction.ts:957](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:957) [table.ts:154](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:154) |\n| 19 | **M · Partly fixed. Ran formatter tests, reasoned through language inheritance.** | The point templates and `plotRole` are used. Default plot text and the state live region can carry `lang=\"en\"`. On a German page, overriding just `plotLabel` removes English marking from the remaining English role and point text. Conversely, translated point text can inherit English from the default label and role. Generated summaries, built-in table cell text, and donut “No data” remain unmarked. Mixed author names do not exempt the surrounding English sentences. Carry language with generated text runs and add localized navigation instructions. **A3, A10, decision 0001, WCAG 3.1.2.** [interaction.ts:1170](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1170) [figure.ts:185](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:185) [table.ts:120](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:120) |\n| 20 | **M · Fixed. Ran.** | Change only series B from `ms` to `s` while A remains in `ms`. The effective shared-unit title changes and both drawn titles now participate in the layout key. The regression passed. **L6, plan 1.5.** [axes.ts:172](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:172) [focus2.test.ts:86](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/focus2.test.ts:86) |\n| 21 | **M · Partly fixed. Reasoned.** | The axe helper separates incomplete results, the focus test checks mark coordinates, and extra states are scanned on line. Spoken text still comes from a DOM attribute. Several named outcomes are never asserted. The five reader/browser rehearsals and the WCAG-by-criterion conformance table with its test check are outstanding. These remain acceptance gaps under **A2, A3, A6, A8, A9 and I3**. [a11y/util.ts:106](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:106) [axe.browser.test.ts:82](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:82) [acceptance/report.md](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/report.md) |\n| 22 | **m · Fixed. Reasoned.** | Switch a multi-line chart into increased contrast or forced colors. Legend and tooltip line samples receive both dash patterns and switch under the matching media query. The implementation addresses the reported mismatch. The plotted-path comparison has a test weakness below. **A5, F9, L2.** [swatch.ts:94](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts:94) [css.ts:167](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:167) |\n\n## 2. Findings in the rewritten paths\n\n1. **B · An assistive adjustment can hang the page. Ran the steps, reasoned through the loop.** Use scatter rows `A0, B1, A2, B3, A4` in x order. Narrow to B at global ordinal 1, then set the native range to 2 through `input` or `change`. `atOrdinal` repeatedly chooses a direction toward 2 using *series-local* stepping. I bounded the experiment and got `1, 3, 1, 3, 1, 3, 1`. The production loop has no bound. Resolve absolute native values directly in global ordinal order, reconcile narrowed mode afterward, and enforce termination. Platforms that deliver native value changes bypass the key handler. Platforms that synthesize Up/Down instead encounter series switching, so the synthetic DOM-event test cannot settle touch-reader behavior. **A2, A3, decision 0001, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:486](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:486) [interaction.ts:530](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:530) [focus.ts:331](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:331)\n\n2. **B · A right-hand toolbar is covered by its own table. Reasoned.** Set `legend:'right'`, then click View as table. The side toolbar and plot are siblings in `.axylo-body`. The opaque table covers that entire body at `z-index:4`. Only the plot becomes inert. A pointer cannot reach Hide table, while keyboard focus can still land on fully covered controls. Put the table and plot in the same column, keep the toolbar outside the overlay, and move focus into the newly opened region. With the default bottom toolbar, opening by keyboard currently leaves focus on a disclosure *after* the table, so the next Tab leaves the chart. **I4, A2, A4, WCAG 2.4.3 and 2.4.11.** [figure.ts:138](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:138) [interaction.ts:1001](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1001) [css.ts:236](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:236)\n\n3. **M · The clearance rule makes hover accuracy depend on pointer speed. Reasoned.** In a wide plot, hover at `(200,120)` with the mark at that x and room on the right. The tooltip can begin at `x=222` and span `y=120`. Move in one event to `(235,120)`. Hit testing enters the old tooltip, `pointerleave` preserves its target, and the plot receives no move. A click on a row selects the old datum. Conversely, a slow approach can keep moving the tooltip away. The presentation cache also rounds pointer coordinates into 8-pixel buckets, so 22 px is a placement-time clearance, not a continuing guarantee. Use a stable, hoverable area outside the picking surface, with a continuous approach from the plot. A reserved readout can serve that purpose whenever a floating placement would cover selectable plot positions. It can then keep its row actions and Escape behavior. **I1, I4.** [interaction.ts:355](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:355) [interaction.ts:732](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:732) [tooltip.ts:174](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:174) [WCAG 1.4.13](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#content-on-hover-or-focus)\n\n4. **M · Focused streaming changes the reader’s value without navigation. Ran the text changes. Speech is unverified.** Each distinct-x append in my fixed-focus example changed `aria-valuetext` through its denominator. With bounded `keep`, the ordinal can also change while the same datum survives. Identical strings are guarded, so it would be incorrect to say that every append rewrites the attribute or that every reader announces it. A reader that voices focused value changes on this path would violate A7. Keep native bounds and selection current. Separate changing collection metadata from the focused datum’s unsolicited updates and provide the current position on navigation. Rehearse idle appends, eviction and a user increment immediately after append on all five specified pairs. **A3, A7, decision 0001.** [interaction.ts:410](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:410) [focus.ts:113](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:113)\n\n5. **M · Data replacement can leave the slider describing a point the plot does not highlight. Reasoned.** Focus the plot with the pointer outside it and call `update({data: …})`. The epoch branch clears `focus`. `writeProxy` computes an initial ref without storing it. `current()` still sees `focus === null`, so the slider describes the new first point while its point ring, tooltip and hover target disappear until another action. Replacement can also suppress an external hover update when the new epoch reuses the old series key and x. Establish one effective focus for the new epoch before writing any presentation, and invalidate hover identity across epochs. **A2, A3, `DatumRef`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:325](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:325) [interaction.ts:420](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:420) [interaction.ts:1233](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1233)\n\n6. **M · Entering the too-small or compact layout loses focus and can leave old decoration. Reasoned.** Focus a point and shrink below the plot threshold. `placeProxy` hides the active input without handing focus to the table disclosure. Switch a hovered or focused chart to `compact:true` and `prepare` nulls `c` before `clear` can call `drawOverlay(null)`. SVG scene drawing leaves the overlay group alone, and Canvas retains overlay state. A static chart can retain the old cursor or outline. `clear` also leaves `mode`, `source`, `pointer`, `dismissed` and `proxyFocused` available to a later full build. Clear the old overlay while its frame exists, reset input state, and hand focus to a surviving control or a programmatically focusable figure without adding a compact tab stop. **A2, C1, WCAG 2.4.3.** [interaction.ts:1161](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1161) [interaction.ts:1276](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1276) [interaction.ts:1292](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1292)\n\n7. **M · Keyboard zoom-in can zoom out. Ran.** On a line with x values `0,10,…,100`, set a supported public window `[40,45]`. The gesture minimum is 20. At center 42.5, the zoom-in calculation returned `[32.5,52.5]`. The toolbar disables Zoom in, but `+` and inward wheel still call `scaled`, which accepts any different result. Require a strictly narrower result for zoom-in and a strictly wider result for zoom-out. Apply the same decision to wheel consumption. **I3, I4.** [focus.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:285) [interaction.ts:629](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:629)\n\n8. **M · Two unavailable plot states expose misleading slider behavior. Ran state and lookup inputs, reasoned through the DOM.** Put a zoomed chart into loading. I obtained `ready=false`, `zoom=true`, `zoomed=true`, `tooSmall=false` with the visible message `Loading chart.` The recovery branch therefore exposes a slider saying `No data to show.` Separately, hide both series on a three-x line. I obtained `ready=true`, native maximum 2, no first ref and no primary at ordinal 1. An adjustment snaps back to zero. Distinguish an actual empty zoom from loading/error, and represent a plot with no readable series accurately while keeping legend recovery available. **L7, A2, A3, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:285) [interaction.ts:413](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:413)\n\n9. **M · Some selectable data have no usable touch target. Reasoned.** Tap a narrow two-series plot, then tap the secondary readout row. The passive readout lets the tap through. Even in a floating tip, a clickable row is an `aria-hidden` plain `div` with no 24 px minimum and no spacing between adjacent choices. On donut, a zero or null slice has no pickable arc, its list item has no action, and keyboard Enter can select it. Provide accessible, touch-sized row or slice actions while preserving the two closed-chart tab stops through the existing composite controls. Close or suspend a pin when the table replaces the plot, including when the disclosure was activated by keyboard without a document `pointerdown`. **I4, A2, F8, WCAG 2.5.8 and 4.1.2.** [tooltip.ts:88](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:88) [figure.ts:126](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:126) [interaction.ts:1098](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1098) [css.ts:154](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:154)\n\n10. **M · Gesture work survives cancellation or a change of owner. Reasoned.** Start a pinch, move, then blur the window or receive `pointercancel` before the queued frame. The callback can still submit `pinchWindow`. During a two-finger pinch, adding finger C and lifting A also leaves B/C using the original A/B baseline. On a nonzoomable plot, a mouse press followed by release outside can leave `down` set because capture was conditional on zoom. Centralize cancellation, release ownership on every exit and cancel the pending frame on cancellation, detach and rebuild. Preserve the final valid move on an ordinary release. **I3, I4, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:783](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:783) [interaction.ts:849](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:849) [interaction.ts:918](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:918)\n\n11. **M · Bar swatches repeat an identical cue at series 33. Reasoned.** Render 33 default-color bar series and compare series 9 and 33. Both use palette slot one, the same square chip and the diagonal pattern. The plotted bars use the same three-pattern cycle. The ninth-series test cannot detect this collision. Extend the shared cue assignment so later cycles remain distinguishable in marks, legend and tooltip. **F9, A5.** [interaction.ts:113](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:113) [swatch.ts:133](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts:133) [bars.ts:107](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:107)\n\n## 3. Tests and coverage\n\n**Tests that can pass with the named behavior broken.** These are reasoned findings from the assertions.\n\n| Test | What can still be broken when it passes |\n|---|---|\n| [focus2.test.ts:68](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/focus2.test.ts:68) | The coarse-double loop breaks on `null` or an unchanged window before its first assertion. The supplied fixture does exactly that. Require a known representable narrowing, check finite ordered endpoints, then check exhaustion. |\n| [review2.browser.test.ts:277](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:277) and [the 40-move test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:619) | The click test counts four selections without checking their identities, and skips its rectangle assertion when no floating tooltip exists. The sweep reads the `hover` callback, allows `ceil(10000 / plotWidth)` indices of error, and uses one small stride. Stale visible text, wrong selected rows and a faster sweep can pass. Assert actual readout text and selected refs with small, large and coalesced moves. |\n| [review2.browser.test.ts:295](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:295) and [the table bounds test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:484) | A clipped fallback passes `isVisible()`. The table test measures vertical bounds once at the opening size. Neither checks hit testing, right-side controls, text zoom, or shrinking an already open table. |\n| [review2.browser.test.ts:322](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:322), [the native range test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:349) and [the secondary-row test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:449) | These prove one anchored mouse halving, two synthetic aligned value changes and a locator click on a floating row. Fixed-width pan, narrowed scatter adjustment, a gradual hover approach and secondary touch selection can all fail. |\n| [interaction.browser.test.ts:130](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:130), [donut legend](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:204), [zoom exclusions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:373) and [pinch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:409) | The donut overlay test checks only tooltip text. The legend accepts a lone value on a fixture where value and percentage coincide. The exclusion test creates only a bar. The pinch test measures an opted-in centered line pinch, never the opt-out, horizontal off-center anchor, cancellation or remaining-finger tap. |\n| [review2.browser.test.ts:502](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:502), [the AX test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:229) and [the stream test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:494) | The page observer samples the final `aria-live` attribute. The 24-stream observer watches initially present live regions and focuses no plot. Neither observes speech. The AX test checks genuine role, number and bounds, but reads the decisive point text from the DOM. |\n| [review2.browser.test.ts:582](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:582) and [the area marker test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:657) | If every plotted SVG path is solid, the dash comparison skips itself. The area test uses line *swatches* as its oracle, so both swatch implementations can agree while disagreeing with the plotted markers. Require the expected renderer-specific marks and compare them directly. |\n| [review2.browser.test.ts:243](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:243) and [axe.browser.test.ts:92](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:92) | The listener test accounts for signal aborts on elements. It never opens a table, creates a pin, queues a pinch, or exercises detach/rebuild. The extra axe test labels two scans “paused” and “zoomed” without asserting Resume or the changed domain first. A broken transition can scan the preceding state again. |\n\n**Coverage by criterion.** This distinguishes exercising a feature from verifying its acceptance outcome. The fixture loop really does run axe on bar, area, scatter and donut. That does not exercise native gestures, spoken navigation or reflow on those types. The relevant fixture definitions and assertions are in [a11y/util.ts:28](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:28), [axe.browser.test.ts:55](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:55) and [keyboard.browser.test.ts:118](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/keyboard.browser.test.ts:118).\n\n| Criterion | Coverage for bar, area, scatter and donut |\n|---|---|\n| **I1** | Area has content and swatch checks, scatter has a pinned-point case, and donut has a slice-content case. Missing across the four is a pointer sweep asserting the type-specific target, displayed rows, edge placement, fallback, Escape and frame deadline. Grouped and horizontal bar picking particularly need a DOM-level check. |\n| **I2** | The click/Enter/Space/pressed-state sequence is line-only. Area and scatter get a click during axe setup. The bar fixture has one series. Donut’s informational list is separately tested and I treat series toggling as inapplicable there. |\n| **I3** | No equivalent-window test across clicks, keys, drag and pinch for continuous bar, area or scatter. Category bar has a negative test. Donut’s ordinary toolbar is checked elsewhere, but the named zoom-exclusion test never creates a donut. |\n| **I4** | Scatter gets a real tap. No complete single-pointer, one-finger scroll and target-size exercise for any of the four, including tooltip rows and arcless donut slices. |\n| **I5** | No per-type first-frame/2.5-second pixel comparison, reduced-motion update step or 24-chart update timing. The line test samples settled CSS animation state. |\n| **I6** | Scatter exercises Pause/Resume and call order. The combined scatter test only requires the paused snapshot to be truthy before checking the resumed result. The frozen-view/control sequence is missing for bar, area and donut. |\n| **A1** | Fixture scans and rendering smoke tests exercise chart structure. They do not check the full accessible name and generated description against each type’s fixture, including ranges, extrema, last values, zone and omissions where applicable. |\n| **A2** | Bar checks End and donut checks focus on one zero slice. Area and scatter have pure navigation checks. None of the four gets the line chart’s complete forward/reverse tab and keyboard walk across states. |\n| **A3** | Bar has an AX role/ordinal assertion, area has generated stack text, and scatter has pure series steps. No full focused-text walk for the four types or recorded native touch-reader adjustment. All five required reader/browser rehearsals remain open. |\n| **A4** | Axe opens the table on all four and donut checks category rows. The full HTML cell, paging, jump, focus, resize and disclosure sequence is missing for bar, area, scatter and donut. |\n| **A5** | Area markers and bar patterns/seams get targeted tests. Those tests do not establish mark-to-swatch agreement in every mode, scatter ties, donut seams or high-count cue uniqueness. The author reports a Canvas seam failure. I did not reproduce browser pixels. |\n| **A6** | No complete 320 CSS px, 400% zoom and text-spacing exercise across the four types and three engines, including open table and readout. |\n| **A7** | No focused-and-unfocused streaming announcement exercise for any of the four. Scatter pin removal and line live-region mutation counts address different outcomes. |\n| **A8** | Basic applicable fixture states are exercised across all four. The additional paused, zoomed, narrow-readout and internal-error scans are line-only. Grouped/all-zero donut and continuous or stacked bar states also need explicit coverage. |\n| **A9** | One release-wide deliverable is required. The acceptance index checks named evidence, but the published WCAG success-criterion table, author obligations, limits and corresponding test-existence check are absent. |\n| **A10** | Foreign-page language assertions are line-based. No equivalent checks for bar, area, scatter or donut summaries, partly translated range text, missing values, table cells or legend text. |\n\n**Verification and contract impact.** I created, edited and deleted no files. I loaded the requested commit’s sources into memory and ran the two named focus suites with filesystem caches disabled. I did not run a browser, screen reader, build, typecheck or full test suite. The test-run tail was:\n\n```text\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  20 passed (20)\n   Start at  05:38:37\n   Duration  293ms (transform 64%, tests 19%, import 16%, worker 1%)\n```\n\nAt the reviewed commit, localized pan controls, jump-error feedback and plot instructions need `Messages` entries such as `panLeft`, `panRight`, `jumpNotFound` and `plotInstructions`. Those keys appeared in the shared checkout **after** `4809516`. The instructions should describe the shipped keys accurately: Up/Down change series and Enter selects. The `DatumRef` comment that categories do not slide also needs correction. Its existing shape can support the DOM remapping fix. For F8, I treated zero and null slices as individually listed even when positive slices are grouped into Other.\n\n**Areas examined and found sound**\n\n- **Toolbar availability and roving focus — reasoned.** Unavailable zoom buttons use `aria-disabled`, remain arrow-focusable, and guard activation. A populated toolbar retains exactly one `tabindex=\"0\"`, including when that item is unavailable.\n- **Ordinary teardown — reasoned.** The implementation uses separate abort lifetimes for the build, document, toolbar, table and tooltip rows. Explicit destroy aborts them and cancels its pending pinch frame.\n- **Wheel ownership — reasoned.** Unfocused, Ctrl-wheel and Meta-wheel paths return before cancellation. The wheel listener is explicitly non-passive.\n- **Table structure — reasoned.** The lazy table has a caption, scoped row and column headers, a named focusable scroll region, bounded pages and guarded pager endpoints.\n- **Ordinary keyboard dismissal — reasoned.** With keyboard ownership, successive Escapes close the tooltip, leave narrowed mode, then pass through. Moving to another target clears dismissal.\n- **Reader note and state channel — reasoned.** The omission note remains readable with `aria-live=\"off\"`. State announcements use a separate polite region with language support.\n- **Ordinary zoom and horizontal-bar projection — ran.** The focus tests passed for center and edge scaling and clamped pan. The upper-quarter horizontal-bar calculation preserved the value under the fingers.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show a518cbb:docs/decisions/0001-plot-interaction-pattern.md && git show a518cbb:docs/02-product-spec.md | sed -n '188,218p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show a518cbb:docs/decisions/0001-plot-interaction-pattern.md && git show a518cbb:docs/02-product-spec.md | sed -n '188,218p'\"","aggregated_output":"# Decision 0001: how the plot is exposed to keyboards and screen readers\n\nStatus: working choice, **not rehearsed with any screen reader**. The plan (M1) called for three candidate patterns to be rehearsed on five screen-reader and browser pairs before choosing. No screen reader can be run in the environment this was built in, so the choice below was made by reasoning and by inspecting Chrome's accessibility tree, and it must be rehearsed by the owner before it is relied on. If rehearsal contradicts it, the plot's roles are internal and can change without touching the public API.\n\n## Candidates\n\n| Pattern | For | Against |\n|---|---|---|\n| A. `role=\"application\"` on the plot, arrow keys handled in script, point text sent to a live region | Used by Recharts and ApexCharts. Full control of keys. | Screen-reader authors discourage `application`; a live region is a second, slower channel; touch screen readers have no arrow keys, so points cannot be reached by swiping. |\n| B. A roving focusable proxy element per point (or one moved around), each with its own label | Each point is a real element with a name. | One element per point does not scale to 100,000 points; a single moved proxy re-announces its role on every move in some readers (from memory, not verified). |\n| C. One native `<input type=\"range\">` laid over the plot, its value the position along x, its `aria-valuetext` the point's text | A native control: desktop readers enter focus mode on it by themselves, arrow keys, Home, End and Page keys work without script, and a change of value text is read without a live region. Touch screen readers expose a native range as an adjustable element, so swiping up and down moves through points (from memory for VoiceOver on iOS and TalkBack; not verified here). One element whatever the number of points. | It is announced as a slider, which is not what a chart is; mitigated by `aria-roledescription` and a label that says what moving it does. Up and Down natively do the same as Right and Left. |\n\n## Choice: C\n\nOne visually transparent native range input covers the plot. It is the plot's single tab stop.\n\n- **Value**: the ordinal of the current x among the visible x positions (for scatter: among visible points in x then y order; for donut: slice order), from `Lookup.ordinal` and `Lookup.count`.\n- **Value text**: by default everything at that x, like the pointer tooltip: the x, then each visible series with its value, then \"point 4 of 120\". After the reader narrows to one series (Up or Down on a keyboard), only that series is read. Escape returns to all series.\n- **Keys**: Left and Right move along x (native). Home, End, Page Up and Page Down native. Up and Down are intercepted to change the series in focus. `+`, `-`, `0` and Shift+arrows zoom and pan. Enter or Space selects (fires `select`). Escape: closes the tooltip first, then leaves single-series mode; otherwise it is not consumed, so a chart inside a dialog does not swallow it.\n- **Touch screen readers**: swiping up or down on the adjustable element moves along x and reads every series at that x; the table is one control away in the toolbar.\n- **Everything else** (legend toggles, zoom buttons, pause, table) is ordinary buttons in one toolbar with roving focus: the chart's second and last tab stop while the table is closed.\n\n## What has to be checked by rehearsal\n\n1. NVDA with Chrome and with Firefox: focus mode is entered on the range without a keystroke; each arrow press reads the new value text once; Up and Down are passed through and the series change is read.\n2. VoiceOver with Safari on macOS: the same, and the role description is read sensibly.\n3. VoiceOver on iOS and TalkBack with Chrome: the element is reachable by touch exploration at the plot's position; swipe up and down move by one point and read it; the toolbar and table are reachable by swiping right.\n4. That a long value text (eight series) is not cut off, and that streaming data does not make the reader speak unless the reader moves.\n### 3.6 Type matrix\n\n| | Line | Area | Bar | Donut | Scatter |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Picking by pointer | Nearest x | Nearest x | The band under the pointer | The slice under the pointer | Nearest point within 24 px; ties go to the later row |\n| Tooltip content | Every visible series at that x | Same, plus the stack total | Every series in that category | Label, value, percentage | The point's series, x and y; coincident points listed, up to eight |\n| Keyboard order | By x, then series | By x, then series | By category, then series | By slice order | By x, then y |\n| Zoom | On time, date and numeric x only | On time, date and numeric x only | On time, date and numeric x only | No | Yes, both axes later; x only in 1.0 |\n| Simplified drawing when dense | F5 | F5 on cumulative sums | No; more bars than pixels raises a hint | No | No in 1.0; above 50,000 points a hint says drawing may be slow |\n| Limit that raises a diagnostic | Eight series | Eight series | Eight series | Eight slices | Eight series |\n| Reference lines and bands | Yes; included in the domain; listed in the summary and table caption | Yes | Yes | No | Yes |\n\n### 3.7 Compact variant\n\n`compact: true` on line, area and bar draws the marks and nothing else: no axes, gridlines, legend, toolbar, table control, zoom or tooltip. It is for a small tile where the page already shows the number and the label.\n\n| ID | Criterion | Verified by |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | A compact chart is a static image with a full text alternative: `role=\"img\"`, an accessible name (as in A1, including AX140 when none is given) and the generated summary as its description (series, x range, minimum, maximum, last value, omissions). It has no tab stop and no pointer-only behavior, so nothing is available to a mouse that is not available to a keyboard. | Accessibility-tree snapshot; a page of 40 has zero added tab stops |\n| C2 | The fidelity rules still hold: zero baseline for bar and area (F1), gaps (F2), diagnostics (F3), simplified drawing (F5), sorting (F11), no motion (I5), scheme from the page (L4). | The same fixtures as the full charts |\n| C3 | It fills its container at any size from 24×16 CSS px up; with no definite height it is 32 px tall. | Size tests |\n| C4 | With more than one series, lines differ by dash as well as color, since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | Two-series fixture |\n| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode |\n\nA compact chart does not give access to every value; the summary is its alternative. An author who needs every value reachable uses the full chart.\n\n### 3.8 What the evidence will and will not show\n\nAutomated checks establish structure: names, roles, focus order, contrast, text. They do not establish that a screen-reader user finds a chart understandable. The only evidence for that in 1.0 is A3's rehearsal by the developer on five reader and browser pairs, recorded as rehearsal. Axylo is built by one person with no access to study participants, so no claim of usability testing with disabled users is made, and the conformance table says so in those words. Reviewers proposed participant testing as a release gate; it is recorded here as a known limit instead.\n\n## 4. Acceptance criteria: the developer's experience\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show a518cbb:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core2.review.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show a518cbb:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core2.review.md'","aggregated_output":"**Four defects block release.** A paused chart can replay rejected or superseded data. A sliding category window can select a different datum from the one announced. Zoom can remove every way to reset the chart. A focused slider can retain a maximum that prevents assistive technology from reaching newly arrived data.\n\n**Ran** identifies results from the repository’s Node-compatible code. **Reasoned** identifies conclusions from tracing the DOM, controller, CSS, or tests. I did not launch a browser or screen reader.\n\n### Blocking\n\n1. **B · Paused appends violate call order and synchronous validation. Reasoned.** Pause a scatter chart, append A, replace the data with B, zoom, then resume. A is replayed against B using the later options and zoom. On a strict chart, an invalid paused append returns successfully. Resume catches the eventual exception, logs it, and discards the remaining queued batches, including valid ones. On aligned charts, even a *rejected* replacement can clear `held` before validation finishes. This extends the strict-rejection issue in the controller review to previously accepted buffered data. Apply each call transactionally to a pending state in call order, validate at the originating call, and freeze only the displayed revision. **I6, plan 1.5.** [chart.ts:257](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:257) · [chart.ts:358](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:358) · [chart.ts:475](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:475)\n\n2. **B · Category eviction changes the identity of keyboard focus. Ran the store and lookup. Reasoned through the slider and selection event.** With categories `A, B, C`, I focused B at ordinal 1 and appended D with `keep: 3`. The new frame contained `B, C, D` in the same epoch. Resolving the saved reference returned **C**, value 2, source row 2. Since the reference still compares equal, the focused slider can continue to say **B** while Enter selects **C**. Preserve the previous category key across a commit and remap it to the new frame before resolving focus, pins, or dismissal. Test both a surviving category and an evicted one. **A3, A7, `DatumRef`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:960](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:960) · [focus.ts:31](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:31) · [store-buffers.ts:129](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:129)\n\n3. **B · An empty zoom removes its own Reset control. Ran the view and zoom arithmetic. Reasoned through control removal.** On a numeric line with observations at `0,1,3,4,96,98,99,100`, one centered zoom produced `[25,75]` with zero value slots. The resulting empty state hides the proxy and removes Zoom out and Reset. Neither `0` nor a click can recover the original view. This makes the controller review’s empty-window finding worse. The same `ready` gate removes Resume from a paused stream that becomes empty, and suppresses the legend and table for an all-zero donut even though its model still contains the labels and zeros. Gate each control on the action it can perform. Keep recovery, Resume, and inspectable rows available in the relevant empty states. **I3, I6, F8, A2, A4, L7.** [chart.ts:605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:605) · [interaction.ts:845](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:845) · [interaction.ts:869](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:869)\n\n4. **B · A focused slider freezes its native bounds as well as its text. Reasoned.** Focus a one-point chart, then append a second point. The reference and mode compare equal, so `writeProxy` returns before updating `max`, `value`, or `aria-valuetext`. A touch-reader increment encounters the old maximum of zero and can produce no `input` event. A physical arrow key happens to repair the bounds in `syncNative`. The same shortcut leaves an obsolete ordinal after eviction, an obsolete count after zoom, or old values, units, series names, and locale after an update. The AT-facing range needs to match each displayed revision. Diff its actual bounds, ordinal, and formatted text, keep unsolicited live announcements separate, and rehearse focused updates on the supported readers. **Decision 0001, A3, A7, WCAG 4.1.2, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:320](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:320) · [interaction.ts:337](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:337)\n\n### Major\n\n5. **M · `keep` does not bound retained memory. Ran the aligned store. Reasoned through controller ownership.** After 1,000 appends with `keep: 3`, the frame held 3 rows and the store reported **1,001 retained rows**. Retiring superseded revisions reduced retention to 3. The controller never calls `retire`. Paused scatter and donut charts additionally keep a copy of every incoming batch until Resume, even with `keep: 1`. Retain the displayed snapshot and the latest accepted state, retire superseded revisions, and apply retention to the pending store as data arrives. Preserve rows still addressable from the displayed frame. **I6, plan 1.5, P7.** [chart.ts:358](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:358) · [chart.ts:383](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:383) · [store.ts:453](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:453)\n\n6. **M · A clamped key can reverse the next assistive action. Reasoned.** Press Home at ordinal 0. The handler saves `intent = 'first'`, but the native value does not change, so no `input` clears it. An assistive increment to 1 then consumes the stale Home and returns to 0. Held keys at an endpoint have the same problem. A direct assistive value-set from 10 to 70 is interpreted as one page; a `change`-only notification has no handler. Also, tabbing onto a hovered plot sets `source = 'keyboard'` before `takeover` can adopt the pointer target. Scope key intent to its native action, reconcile the requested absolute ordinal once across supported event paths, and take over the pointer datum before changing source. **Decision 0001, A2, A3, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:432](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:432) · [interaction.ts:442](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:442) · [interaction.ts:458](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:458)\n\n7. **M · Keyboard exploration drops information available to the pointer. Ran.** With A at x=0 and 2 and hidden B at x=1, lookup counted three slots and the pointer reported “No observation” at 1. Right jumped directly from 0 to 2. For coincident scatter points, the pointer target contained two refs while the keyboard-created target contained one. On alternating scatter series, switching from A to B and pressing Right landed back on A. For a stacked area with values 2 and 3, the tooltip total was 5 and the all-series value text omitted it. On an incomplete stack, the text repeated “incomplete” per series and omitted the total. Use the lookup’s visible ordinal order and tooltip model for all-series navigation and text. Preserve the chosen series in narrowed mode. **Decision 0001, A2, A3, I1, §3.6.** [focus.ts:23](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:23) · [focus.ts:63](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:63) · [focus.ts:141](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:141) · [interaction.ts:381](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:381)\n\n8. **M · Panning and selection lack single-pointer equivalents. Reasoned.** Zoom in, then try to move the window right using taps or clicks alone. The toolbar only scales around the center or resets. Shift+Right, a drag, or a two-finger gesture can reach ranges that the buttons cannot. A mouse click and Enter/Space emit `select`; a touch tap only pins. A fresh mouse user also cannot explicitly select a secondary aligned series at the same x as the primary series. Provide single-click pan controls and a selectable datum or tooltip row that works with touch, mouse, and keyboard. **I3, I4, WCAG 2.5.1 and 2.5.7.** [interaction.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:662) · [interaction.ts:691](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:691) · [interaction.ts:845](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:845)\n\n9. **M · Enabled zoom controls can do nothing or produce a zero-width window. Ran.** For `[0,100]` with two or three aligned x positions, the computed minimum width was 200 or 100. Zoom in returned `null` at full view. Drag accepts half that minimum, so one input method can reach a range another cannot. On scatter `[10¹⁶,10¹⁶+4]`, the second halving produced two identical endpoints. The focused wheel calls `preventDefault()` even when zoom cannot move. Category line, area, and bar all returned `false` from `zoomApplies`, although §3.6 gives the category exclusion specifically to bars. Use one representable minimum across gestures, enforce strictly ordered finite endpoints, disable exhausted controls, and consume the wheel only for an effective change. Implement ordinal zoom for supported category charts. **I3, I4, §3.6.** [focus.ts:282](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:282) · [focus.ts:298](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:298) · [interaction.ts:519](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:519) · [interaction.ts:656](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:656)\n\n10. **M · Gesture cancellation and pinch anchoring are inconsistent. Reasoned; ran the horizontal projection arithmetic.** Start a captured drag and press Escape. The document handler clears `down` without releasing capture or consuming the active cancellation, so a containing dialog can close too. There is no lost-capture or window-blur cleanup. A second non-touch pointer overwrites the drag, and a remaining pinch finger can be treated as a fresh tap after the other lifts. On a horizontal continuous bar axis, the pinch calculation measures the fraction downward while the scale increases upward. In a `[0,100]` projection, halving at the upper quarter moved the value under the fingers from 75 to 87.5. Give each gesture explicit pointer ownership, cancel and release it on every exit, suppress post-pinch taps, and derive the anchor fraction from the projection. **I3, I4, decision 0001.** [interaction.ts:609](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:609) · [interaction.ts:635](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:635) · [interaction.ts:737](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:737) · [interaction.ts:754](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:754)\n\n11. **M · A pinned scatter tooltip survives removal of its marks. Ran the lookup distinction. Reasoned through commit.** Tap to pin a scatter point, then programmatically zoom it out of view. Commit keeps the old target if `lookup.tooltip(oldTarget)` returns any rows. That lookup can format a source row outside the current view. I also obtained two tooltip rows for two previously coincident points after hiding both series in a new lookup. Validate pinned refs using their visible ordinals, rebuild the coincident set and count for the displayed revision, and dismiss when the pinned datum leaves it. **I1, A7, `PickTarget`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:977](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:977) · [scatter.ts:159](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter.ts:159)\n\n12. **M · Tooltip positioning can cover a mark, escape the viewport, or be clipped. Reasoned.** Hover a chart under `transform: scale(2)`. Pointer deltas are viewport pixels passed to a layout-pixel lookup, and the tooltip translation mixes viewport bounds with unscaled `offsetWidth` and `offsetHeight`. In an overflow-clipped card, a candidate can fit the viewport but extend beyond the card. When no candidate fits, the last branch still shows a clamped rectangle, even across the active mark or when the tooltip is taller than the viewport. Scrolling a pinned or keyboard-focused chart does not recheck placement. Convert coordinates consistently, intersect clipping bounds, exclude the mark and focus ring, and use the readout when no candidate fits. **I1, A2, A6, WCAG 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:296](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:296) · [interaction.ts:529](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:529) · [tooltip.ts:93](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:93)\n\n13. **M · The narrow readout covers the controls and disappears when approached. Reasoned.** In the 260 px tile, hover a point and move onto the readout. `pointerleave` exempts only the floating tooltip, so the readout disappears. When touch-pinned, the opaque readout sits directly over the toolbar at `z-index: 3`; tapping it counts as inside and cannot activate the button underneath. Keyboard dismissal also persists too long: dismiss at A, move to B, then return to A, and A is still suppressed. Reserve a reachable readout area, include it in hover persistence, and clear dismissal on the first target change from either input source. **I1, I4, WCAG 1.4.13 and 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:534](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:534) · [interaction.ts:580](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:580) · [tooltip.ts:125](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:125) · [css.ts:142](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:142)\n\n14. **M · Keyboard focus can be entirely invisible on a donut. Ran the overlay and layout. Reasoned about clipping.** Tab to a donut whose first slice has value zero and whose second slice is positive. In a 320×200 layout, the plot occupied `(0,0,320,200)`. The first slice had no anchor and produced no overlay. The remaining CSS focus outline is drawn outside that exact rectangle and clipped by the plot’s `overflow: hidden`; the native input is transparent. Draw the plot ring inside its bounds and visibly identify the focused legend entry for an arcless slice. **F8, A2, WCAG 2.4.7.** [focus.ts:240](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:240) · [css.ts:128](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:128) · [css.ts:174](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:174)\n\n15. **M · Opening the table overflows fixed cards and moves auto-height neighbors. Reasoned.** Open a table in a short fixed-height card. The code freezes the plot at its former pixel height, then inserts the table and pager below the controls. A clipping card hides them; an unclipped card can cover the next chart. In an auto-height stack, following charts move. A 100 px plot can also receive a 160 px scroll region because of `Math.max(160, height)`. The 24-chart test compares fixed outer tile rectangles, which remain equal even when their contents overlap. Allocate a bounded, responsive table area and test actual content bounds after opening, resizing, and text zoom. **A4, A6, WCAG 1.4.4, 1.4.10 and 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:786](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:786) · [interaction.ts:816](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:816) · [interaction.browser.test.ts:575](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:575)\n\n16. **M · An open table announces incoming data. Reasoned.** Leave page 1 open with 200 rows and append row 201. Rendering changes the polite region from “Page 1 of 2” to “Page 1 of 3” without reader action. Page clamping after eviction can do the same. The 24-stream test opens no tables and observes only live regions present at setup. Keep the visible count current and announce page changes only from reader-initiated paging or jumping. **A7, WCAG 4.1.3.** [table.ts:64](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:64) · [table.ts:132](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:132) · [interaction.browser.test.ts:467](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:467)\n\n17. **M · One `tabindex=\"0\"` does not guarantee that focus survives a render. Reasoned.** Focus legend B, then update wide fields from `[A,B]` to `[B,A]`. The renderer moves B using `insertBefore`; ordinary removal and reinsertion can drop focus. Its restoration path runs only when the key disappears. With focus in the jump field, disabling the table removes the active element without a handoff. Shrinking to one page likewise hides the focused pager. Preserve or restore the active control after reordering, and move focus to the disclosure, scroll region, or another surviving control before removing a focused subtree. **A2, A4, WCAG 2.4.3.** [toolbar.ts:94](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/toolbar.ts:94) · [toolbar.ts:135](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/toolbar.ts:135) · [interaction.ts:795](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:795) · [table.ts:123](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:123)\n\n18. **M · “Jump to” can reject the displayed x or jump to another one. Ran the table model. Reasoned through the field.** The model accepted canonical ISO dates and instants, but rejected its own displayed `May 31, 2026` and `May 31, 2026, 12:00 AM UTC`. The field also rejects the displayed English `900,000`, while removing all whitespace turns `1 2` into 12. Its parser captures the x kind when the table opens, so changing a numeric axis to categories can coerce a valid category such as `002` into a different target. Invalid input only sets `aria-invalid`. Use the current model’s parser, preserve exact category labels, and provide an accepted-format example and visible, associated error text. **A4, A6, WCAG 3.3.1 and 3.3.2.** [interaction.ts:777](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:777) · [table.ts:144](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:144)\n\n19. **M · The plot ignores translation keys and exposes English under the page language. Ran the value formatter. Reasoned through language inheritance.** Overrides for `pointAll`, `seriesValue`, and `position` still produced `0: a 2; b 3. Point 1 of 2.` The role description uses `typeLine` directly instead of `plotRole`. On a German page, the default slider label, role description, value text, generated summary, and polite state announcement can all inherit German. The note’s language also depends on *all three* note keys being untranslated, regardless of which sentence is displayed. Apply the existing message templates and assign language where each generated string is exposed. Give the range a label or description explaining navigation. **A3, A10, decision 0001.** [focus.ts:119](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:119) · [interaction.ts:942](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:942) · [chart.ts:756](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:756) · [figure.ts:182](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:182)\n\n20. **M · An axis can retain the wrong unit after an update. Ran.** I built a wide line with A and B both in `ms`, then changed only B to `s`. The production view and layout-input paths produced `Value (ms)` and `Value`, respectively, but `sameKey` returned `true`. The controller can therefore keep a milliseconds axis title while the tooltip and table use the new units. Include the effective axis title and shared unit in the layout key. **L6, plan 1.5.** [axes.ts:100](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:100) · [axes.ts:165](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:165)\n\n21. **M · The accessibility tests cannot establish several claimed outcomes. Reasoned from the tests.** `axNode` gets role, name, value, and maximum from Chrome, but gets its decisive spoken-text assertion directly from `getAttribute('aria-valuetext')`. The focus-obscuration assertion compares areas; a small tooltip can pass while completely covering the focused mark. The axe helper scans `body` with default rules and no explicit rule exclusions, but counts `incomplete` among rules that “ran.” The fixture loop covers four states and omits paused, zoomed, narrow-readout, and internal-error states. The pinch opt-out and donut overlay tests also omit the outcomes named in their titles. Assert computed AX output where available, report inconclusive rules separately, test actual intersections and state transitions, and record the five reader/browser rehearsals. I found no A9 conformance table with a test-existence check. **A2, A3, A6, A8, A9, I3.** [util.ts:97](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:97) · [util.ts:118](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:118) · [axe.browser.test.ts:62](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:62) · [keyboard.browser.test.ts:214](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/keyboard.browser.test.ts:214)\n\n### Minor\n\n22. **m · High-contrast line swatches do not repeat the plotted dash. Reasoned.** Enable forced colors or increased contrast on a multi-line chart. The plotted lines switch to their contrast dash, while legend and tooltip swatches read only `cue.dash.normal`. Marker shapes still provide a cue, but the legend can show a solid sample for a dashed line. Bind swatches to the same normal and contrast patterns as the marks and inspect both at eight and more than eight series. **A5, F9, L2.** [swatch.ts:59](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts:59) · [css.ts:79](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:79)\n\n### Verification and interpretation\n\nI made no file changes. `npm run typecheck` passed. I ran the focus, axes, and reader suites in Vitest’s thread pool with filesystem caches disabled. The last lines were:\n\n```text\n Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  33 passed (33)\n   Start at  04:06:58\n   Duration  568ms (transform 48%, tests 40%, import 11%, worker 1%)\n```\n\nI treated §3.6’s “Yes” for line and area zoom as including categories. I3 explicitly mandates time, date, and numeric axes. I treated F8’s donut legend as an informational slice list and I2’s toggles as Cartesian series controls. The current checkout already provides the translation keys needed for finding 19. No change to `contracts.ts` or `public.ts` is required. Browser pixels, native event sequences across engines, actual announcements, and 400% reflow remain unverified.\n\n### Areas examined and found sound\n\n- **Ordinary zoom arithmetic — ran.** Halving around 0, 50, and 100 preserved the anchor, doubling returned to full view, and pan clamped at both edges. Ten thousand reciprocal wheel pairs drifted by about `1.4×10⁻¹⁴` on `[0,100]`. Calendar-date scaling preserved UTC positions.\n- **Ordinary wheel and page gestures — reasoned.** The wheel listener is explicitly non-passive. Unfocused, Ctrl-wheel, and Meta-wheel paths return before cancellation. Default touch handling allows page pan and pinch, and opt-in chart pinch retains one-finger page pan.\n- **Table semantics and laziness — ran the reader suite; inspected the DOM builder.** The aligned table addresses a distant page directly, renders at most 100 rows, retains hidden-series columns, and limits rows to the current x range. The DOM supplies a caption, scoped column and row headers, a named focusable scroll region, and guarded pager endpoints.\n- **Ordinary toolbar traversal and sizing — reasoned.** A populated stable toolbar has one tabbable button. Arrows wrap, Home/End reach the ends, Tab and Shift+Tab leave, and removing focused Reset hands focus to a surviving neighbor. Buttons specify a 24×24 CSS px minimum. Only the table headers are sticky.\n- **Hidden-series presentation — reasoned.** Legend toggles expose `aria-pressed`, retain the normal text color, and add a strike-through and hollow swatch. The table disclosure exposes `aria-expanded` and references the mounted table while open.\n- **Visible tooltip content — ran the lookup; inspected rendering.** “No observation” and “No data” remain distinct. The floating tooltip and readout share the same row renderer, overflow count, and stack-total rendering.\n- **Ordinary Escape and teardown — reasoned.** With the proxy focused, successive Escapes close the tooltip, leave single-series mode, then pass to the page. Explicit destruction removes the interaction layer’s document listeners and cancels its pending pinch frame.\n- **Compact interaction, motion, and the reader note — reasoned.** Compact charts omit the proxy and toolbar and install no plot interaction handlers. The reviewed styles introduce no animation. The full-chart note remains available as text with `aria-live=\"off\"`, independently of the polite state-change region.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
