ts 84 passed | 1 skipped (85)`.\n- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts`:** `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 28 passed (28)`.\n\nLogs are `p9-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\nNo contract changes needed.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, sixth pass: report\n\nNothing is committed. The browser acceptance suite (SVG) is at 538 of 551, up from 899/37 failures across all suites at d8b4150. The 13 that still fail are three groups: a test-procedure limit, a conflict between the decision's geometry and the test path, and a browser timing limit. Each is explained below with a suggested way out. I did not swap the shared `dist`: old-code checks used the privately built 0e5aa29 bundle through my `AXYLO_BUNDLE` switch.\n\n### Decision 0004 revision 2, implemented as written\n- **`src/dom/tooltip.ts`, rewritten.**\n  - **Placement:** the position comes from the datum alone: the box of its active marks, enlarged by the ring's reach (`RING_REACH` = 9 px).\n  - **Candidates:** above, below, right, left; horizontal bars right, left, above, below; donut tries the hole first. A candidate is valid only wholly inside the plot rectangle (inset 4 px, clear of the plot outline), the viewport and every clipping ancestor, overlapping neither the box nor any control of the figure.\n  - **Rule 6:** rows are dropped into \"+N more\"; if nothing is valid with one row, the candidate that overlaps the box least is used, inside the plot.\n  - **Hovered vs pinned:** a hovered tooltip has `pointer-events: none` and text rows; a pinned one takes events and its rows are buttons of at least 24 × 24 px.\n  - **`strip()`:** running text \"x: series value; …; +N more\" fitted to two lines; entries become 24 px buttons when pinned.\n- **`src/dom/interaction.ts`.**\n  - **Pinning:** a click pins, as a tap already did. A pinned tooltip ignores moves until Escape, a click elsewhere, a keyboard move, or its datum leaving.\n  - **Holding on scatter and donut:** the datum is held while the pointer is inside the rectangle its tooltip had (computed in the plot's own move handler).\n  - **Readout mode:** a class on the figure; the strip and the axis area under the plot count as hoverable.\n- **`src/core/controller.ts`, readout mode by layout.** The plot rectangle without the strip, laid out in the plot's whole column (`room`, from `chart.ts` `measure()`), is under 240 × 140. One more condition: the plot must keep the L8 minimum of 80 px beside the strip.\n  - Without that condition, the 24 tiles of 340 × 200 in I5 fell into the too-small fallback and drew nothing.\n  - With it, L8 by height and I5 both pass.\n  - The decision does not depend on the strip, so it does not oscillate.\n- **Figure and CSS:** the readout element now sits in the plot's column under the plot (`figure.ts`). The strip is two reserved lines (`css.ts`, figure section).\n- **Rings are drawn inside the plot's box** (`core/focus.ts` `buildOverlay`), so the ring at the last point and at the top of a donut is painted. The A2 focus-indicator tests pass.\n\n### Other items\n- **A7 bar:** the category remap now remaps the text's own datum too, so a sliding window no longer rewrites it. New test fails on 0e5aa29 and passes now.\n- **JSON in the page:** the source was `note.dataset.segments = JSON.stringify(runs)` in `figure.ts`. That comparison is now kept in memory. The distribution browser run passes (30/30).\n- **L1 late font:** the cause was that `FontFace.load()` followed by `document.fonts.add()` never fires `loadingdone`. A font probe in the text layer is watched with a ResizeObserver; when it changes size, the fonts are invalidated and everything is laid out again (`chart.ts`, `css.ts`). The L1 late-font tests pass.\n- **L8 short summary:** first sentence, at most two lines, ellipsis beyond (line clamp in `css.ts`). L8 tests pass.\n- **L4:** theme changes are now resolved and written inside the observer's callback, with the canvas still repainted once through the scheduler. The class, style and data-theme triggers pass on all six kinds.\n- **Wiring from the scene and lookup author:**\n  - `buildLookup` gets the device pixel ratio, and on scatter it is in the lookup's cache key.\n  - The donut focus outline uses `donutGeometry`'s adjusted angles.\n  - T-pointer-scatter and T-dense-donut pass.\n- **Item 5:** the reader's `seriesNotDrawnSentence` and runs were wired in pass 5 and still are. **AX143** passes `chartType`, `xKind` and `horizontal`.\n- **Item 6:** `focus.ts` takes the total from the lookup's tooltip model and computes no net total.\n\n### Still failing (13), and why\n1. **I1 \"readout mode … 139 px high\", 5 types.** Entering readout mode reserves the strip, so the plot jumps from about 140 px straight to about 92 px; no plot height exists in between. The test's bisection (`plotTo`) stops on whichever side it probed last, and here it is the 140.07 px side. At 139 px the library is in readout mode. The width bracket passes. This needs a test change: for example, report the last readout-side height of the bisection.\n2. **I1 bar hover.** The fixture's bars reach within about 40 px of the plot top, so neither \"above\" nor \"below\" fits. The tooltip goes beside the box, and the straight path crosses into the next band at step 1 (\"rows changed\"). Under rule 3 only an approach across the reading axis keeps the datum.\n3. **I1 donut hover.** \"Hole first\" puts the tooltip in the hole. The straight path from the Travel slice crosses the Rent slice (steps 10–18) and the empty hole before entering the rectangle. The tooltip shown last on the way was Rent's, which is narrower, so at step 24 the pointer is outside Rent's rectangle and nothing is held. Rule 3 holds a datum only inside its tooltip's rectangle.\n4. **L4, 6 kinds: only the `prefers-color-scheme` part fails.** Probe: after `emulateMedia({colorScheme:'dark'})`, `matchMedia(...).matches` is already true in the next rAF, but Chrome dispatches the `change` event one frame later. No JavaScript can resolve the theme earlier. A fix for charts with `color-scheme: light dark` would be for theme resolution (`src/theme`, not mine) to write `light-dark(light, dark)` values, which the browser switches by itself. Otherwise the test would need to wait two frames.\n\nFor items 2 and 3 I need your decision: change the test path, or change the decision (for example, no \"hole first\" on donut, or a hold along the path).\n\n### Expectations of my own tests changed for revision 2\nThese now assert the revised rules:\n- **The tooltip's position:**\n  - \"four plot edges\" no longer requires the pointer to be outside the tooltip; it asserts the tooltip does not move while the datum is unchanged.\n  - The scale(2) test checks the tooltip stays inside the plot instead of centred on the bar.\n- **Pinning and rows:**\n  - A click pins; a hovered row is text, and a pinned row is the button that selects.\n  - The hover-event sequence is adjusted for click-pinning.\n  - The coincident-count test accepts rows plus \"+N more\" adding up to nine.\n- **Readout mode:**\n  - The narrow-tile and axe readout tests use a 220 px tile, since readout mode now starts below 240 px.\n  - The readout text may end in \"+N more\".\n\nThere is also a new L4 first-frame test in `test/browser/chart/theme.browser.test.ts`. It passes on old code too, so it is a guard only.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- **`src/theme/css.ts`** (figure section only): tooltip, strip, choice buttons, font probe, summary line clamp.\n- **No layout changes.** I tried a `minimum` option in `src/layout` during the pass, then removed it, and `src/layout` and `test/layout` match HEAD. The final full run happened before that removal, with the option present but unused.\n\n### Runs (last lines)\n- **Type check:** exit 0.\n- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test --exclude '**/acceptance/**'`:** `Test Files 1 failed | 45 passed (46)`, `Tests 1 failed | 775 passed (776)`. The one failure is the kept memory test in `data/streaming-storage`.\n- **My browser directories, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 187 passed (187)`.\n- **My browser directories, canvas:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 187 passed (187)`.\n- **`AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance` (SVG):** `Test Files 2 failed | 11 passed (13)`, `Tests 13 failed | 538 passed (551)`.\n- **`AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts`:** `Test Files 4 passed (4)`, `Tests 30 passed (30)`.\n\nLogs are `r1-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, seventh pass: report\n\nAll five items are done. Browser acceptance on SVG now passes in full, 555 of 555, and both items you asked me to confirm (I5 and L1 bar at 200% text) pass in it. Nothing is committed; I did not swap the shared `dist` (old-code checks used private builds of 4504ca4 via `AXYLO_BUNDLE`).\n\n### 1. Rule 3b: a rest holds the datum along the corridor (`src/dom/interaction.ts`)\n- **Rest:** a pointer that stays within 2 CSS px for 250 ms, measured with the events' own timestamps, has rested.\n- **Where it applies:** when the datum's floating tooltip is not across the reading axis (beside a bar or stack; always on scatter and donut).\n- **Hold:** after a rest, the datum is held while the pointer is inside the convex hull of the resting point and the tooltip's rectangle. Leaving the hull resumes picking on that same move; a pointer that never rested is never held. The tooltip stays pointer-transparent and does not move.\n- **One adjustment:** the corridor opens on the first move after the rest, even a move of 2 px or less. Without that, a datum resting exactly on a band edge (the acceptance bar probe) changed on the first 1 px step.\n- **Tests:** five browser tests in `test/browser/chart/review6.browser.test.ts`:\n  - bar after a rest;\n  - bar without a rest, where the datum changes;\n  - leaving the rectangle away from the corridor;\n  - a fast sweep after a rest elsewhere;\n  - donut with the tooltip in the hole.\n\n  On 4504ca4 the three that need the hold fail; the no-rest and sweep tests also pass on old code, so they only guard.\n\n### 2. L4 on a prefers-color-scheme change, fixed in CSS (`src/theme/`)\n- **Stylesheet (`css.ts`):** the `.axylo` private defaults are now `light-dark(light, dark)`, so they switch in the frame the media query does. Fixed sets remain under `[data-axylo-scheme=\"light\"]` and `[data-axylo-scheme=\"dark\"]`. The comment says `light-dark()` is supported by the current and previous major versions of the four browsers in spec 2.3.\n- **Resolution (`resolve.ts`):** when the chart's computed `color-scheme` is anything but `normal` and no `--axylo-background` decides, no `data-axylo-scheme` is written. The per-series properties were already references, not frozen colours.\n  - With `color-scheme: normal` or `--axylo-background`, it works as before.\n  - Forced colours and `prefers-contrast` are unchanged and still pass in the render suite.\n- **Canvas:** it still repaints when the change event arrives, one frame behind; a comment in `controller.ts` says so, and AX141 is judged then.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `test/theme/review.test.ts` checks the generated stylesheet.\n  - `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` emulates the media change under `color-scheme: light dark` and reads the mark colour in the first rAF. It fails on 4504ca4.\n- **Tests changed:** three render tests and two of my chart tests expected the attribute in \"page sets color-scheme\" cases. They now expect none, which is the design change, not a loosened check.\n\n### 3. Two-tone focus ring (palette review B1)\n- **Datum ring (`core/focus.ts`):** a 4 px background-colour surround with the 2 px focus colour on top, i.e. 1 px of background on each side. Corners are closed, the ring is kept inside the plot's box, and the tooltip's avoid-box grows by the surround (`RING_REACH` 10).\n- **Plot outline (`css.ts`):** an inset `box-shadow` in the background colour under the 2 px outline. `forced-color-adjust: none` keeps it in forced colours, where both tokens are already system colours.\n- **Tests:**\n  - New browser test (`review6`): dark scheme, a bar of each of the 8 dark series colours, painted pixels at device pixel ratio 2. Crossing the ring finds background, then focus colour, then background, and the ring really crosses the neighbouring bar. It fails on 4504ca4 and passes on both renderers.\n  - `test/core/focus.test.ts`: its expectation changed from 4 focus rules to 4 surround rules plus 4 focus rules.\n- The acceptance A2 tests still pass.\n\n### 4. Untitled chart named by its target's id (React review C6)\n- `Host.targetId`, from `root.id` in `chart.ts`, is used for the diagnostic chart name and for the internal-error delivery. The allocated id stays for the DOM relationships.\n- Node tests in `snapshot.test.ts`: \"sessions\" when the target has that id, the allocated id otherwise. `test/core/host.ts` has a new `targetId` option.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- `src/theme/css.ts`: the token blocks and the ring surround.\n- `src/theme/resolve.ts`: the scheme attribute rule only.\n- `test/theme/review.test.ts`, `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` (new), and the expectations in `test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts` and `review.browser.test.ts`.\n- `test/browser/chart/util.ts`: `AXYLO_BUNDLE` now also reaches the render suites, without the renderer switch.\n- `palette.ts` and `test/theme/palette.test.ts` show as modified in the tree, but those are the palette author's changes, not mine.\n\n### Runs (last lines, final build)\n- **Type check:** clean.\n  - In the chained run it failed once with `packages/react/src/index.ts(114,50): error TS2554`, while the React author was editing that file.\n  - Re-run afterwards: `tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit && tsc -p docs/api && tsc -p packages/react && tsc -p tests/dist`, no errors.\n- **Node suite without acceptance:** `Test Files 2 failed | 44 passed (46)`, `Tests 2 failed | 791 passed (793)`. Neither failure is mine:\n  - the kept memory test (`data/streaming-storage`);\n  - `scene/scene.test.ts` \"keeps generated geometry finite and clipped across independent chart states\", which fails identically on a clean HEAD tree (2727a30).\n- **My browser directories, SVG:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n- **My browser directories, canvas:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n- **Render (browser):** `Test Files 6 passed | 1 skipped (7)`, `Tests 86 passed | 1 skipped (87)`.\n- **Theme (Node):** `Test Files 3 passed (3)`, `Tests 52 passed (52)`.\n- **Browser acceptance, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 555 passed (555)`.\n\nLogs are `s3-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a8a13825a6a59c62a. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Tree-shaking work package: report\n\nNothing is committed. `dist` was last built from the final tree, which type-checks. I made one restructuring with no intended behaviour change. All four steps are done. I ran full verification twice: at the end of step 1, and once more on the finished tree. Steps 2, 3 and 4 were verified together (Node tests at each change; the browser suites only on the final build), not one step at a time.\n\n### Baseline (measured by me at the start; the brief's 99.47 KiB predates commit e9449a6)\nMeasured from the packed tarballs with `scripts/size.mjs`:\n- everything: 107,960 B gzip (105.43 KiB)\n- line only: 107,835 B (105.31 KiB)\n- script tag: 108,088 + 5,094 CSS = 110.53 KiB\n- React adapter: 1,671 B (1.63 KiB)\n\nAt baseline the other kinds alone were about 107.6 KB each. That figure is from a source rebuild, not the tarballs, because nothing was shaken.\n\n### Step 1: per-chart composition\n**Map for a reviewer:**\n- `src/core/composition.ts` defines the `Composition` interface: normalize, openStore, view, scene, lookup, reader parts, interaction parts, and SVG and canvas mark handlers.\n- `src/kinds/{line,area,bar,scatter,donut}.ts` are plain object literals of function references. `src/kinds/index.ts` holds `COMPOSITIONS`.\n- `index.ts`: `line()` calls `createChart(LINE, …)`.\n- `core/chart.ts`: `createChart(composition, …)` uses `svgRendererWith` / `canvasRendererWith(composition.*)` and `createInteraction(composition.interaction, …)`.\n- `core/controller.ts`: new `controllerFor(composition, …)`. `createController(kind, …)` is kept for the tests and maps through `COMPOSITIONS`.\n\n**Per-shape entry points (the old dispatchers are kept as thin wrappers for tests and for `validate`):**\n- `data/normalize.ts`: `normalizeAligned`, `normalizePoints`, `normalizeDonut`. The stores and `reader/x.ts` now call these directly.\n- `data/store.ts`: `openAlignedStore`.\n- `data/store-unaligned.ts`: `openPointStore`, `openDonutStore`.\n- `view/index.ts`: `buildAlignedView`, `buildScatterView`, `buildDonutView`.\n- `scene/index.ts`: `cartesianScene` plus `line`/`area`/`bar`/`scatter` layers and scenes, and `donutScene`.\n- `lookup/index.ts`: `*LookupFor` functions.\n- `reader`: `readerWith(parts)`, with `alignedReader`, `scatterReader` and `donutReader`; the table is split per shape.\n- `core/focus.ts`: `overlayWith(targetMarks)`, with aligned, scatter and donut target marks.\n- `dom/interaction.ts`: `InteractionParts` (overlay, swatch, `stepInSeries`, `donutSliceList`).\n- `dom/swatch.ts`: `swatchPattern`, so bar pattern drawing is reached only from `barSwatch`.\n- `render/svg.ts` and `render/canvas.ts`: per-mark handler tables. `createSvgRenderer` and `createCanvasRenderer` still have every handler.\n\n**How the ESM ships:** I kept one prebundled file per condition, and made it tree-shakeable.\n- I measured both options. With all import-time work removed, prebundled and a module graph (one file per source module, `sideEffects` false) came out within 25 B for every kind.\n- The module graph was 5.7 KB better for `validate` alone, but only while the stylesheet template still did work at import.\n- I chose prebundled because it leaves `exports`, `files`, the declarations and the package-shape tests unchanged.\n\n**Proof that it shakes:** I removed every piece of import-time work:\n- marker polygons are now built lazily;\n- computed constants (2π, 2⁻²⁰, squares) became literals;\n- the registry became plain data, with the message composed in `createDiagnostic`;\n- the option-name lists are written out instead of spread;\n- `Intl.Segmenter` is created on first use;\n- the time-interval table is built lazily;\n- `TOKEN_BINDINGS` is no longer `Object.freeze`d (readonly by type only; nothing mutates it);\n- the stylesheet is a literal (step 2).\n\n**New test `tests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts` (11 tests, all pass):**\n- Importing `axylo` only for its effects, with `ignoreAnnotations` set so esbuild ignores `sideEffects`, bundles to 0 bytes.\n- For each kind, the bundle must contain its own markers and none of the other kinds'. The markers survive minification:\n  - each kind: `kind:\"<k>\",normalize:`\n  - area: `.upper`\n  - bar: `axylo-pattern-`\n  - scatter: `.minX`\n  - donut: `__other__`\n  - aligned storage: `adoptNormalized`, which must be absent from scatter and donut\n- Each marker is first required in its own kind's bundle, so a marker lost to a rename fails the test instead of passing everything.\n\n**Sizes at the end of step 1** (source rebuilt with the release settings, before CSS minification and instrumentation removal): everything 109,948, line 92,878, area 94,874, bar 94,086, scatter 88,066, donut 81,106.\n\n### Step 2: stylesheet minified once\n- New `src/theme/minify.ts` removes only comments and layout whitespace. It keeps commas, colons, values and strings, and drops the `;` before `}`.\n- `scripts/build.mjs` substitutes the minified literal for `theme/css.ts` in `axylo.js` and `axylo.iife.min.js`, and writes the same text to `dist/axylo.css`.\n- Development files keep `css.ts` as written. I checked that `axylo.dev.js` is byte-identical to a plain `__DEV__: 'true'` rebuild, which the docs guard needs.\n- `build.mjs` now exports `stylesheets()`, `stylesheetPlugin()`, `PRODUCTION` and `DEVELOPMENT`, and only builds when run directly.\n- Stylesheet: 19,977 B → 13,917 B; gzip 5,094 B → 2,886 B.\n- New `packages/axylo/test/theme/minify.test.ts` parses both forms into the same rule tree in order (more than 50 rules and 150 declarations), checks that property names match, and tests idempotence and edge cases.\n- The licence test's origin rule now accepts \"generated from X through Y\". `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` was updated to match.\n\n### Step 3: production instrumentation removed\n- New `src/core/instrument.ts` is the one place for the `__bench` and `__dev` hooks, `StageCounter`, the `Probe` interface and `describe()` (with the line `kept` indexes).\n- The harness's future needs (run starts, the plot rectangle, owned bytes) go in `Probe` and `attachHooks` there.\n- The controller guards with `__DEV__ || (typeof __BENCH__ !== 'undefined' && __BENCH__)`. The `typeof` keeps the acceptance `production.test.ts` working, since it defines only `__DEV__`.\n- `__BENCH__` is declared in `core/globals.d.ts` and is false in every shipped file.\n- AX199 recovery is untouched.\n- Every browser suite loads the dev builds (`axylo.iife.js` and the dev bundles), which still have the hooks. Production-page tests already waited by frames, so no test was changed.\n- Saving: about 650–720 B gzip.\n\n**The define the benchmark build needs:**\n- Its production IIFE: `define: { __DEV__: 'false', __BENCH__: 'true' }`. `__bench` is attached when `globalThis.__AXYLO_BENCH__ === true`, as before.\n- To match shipped bytes otherwise, also add `plugins: [stylesheetPlugin(minified)]`, imported from `scripts/build.mjs`.\n- Its dev IIFE needs no change.\n- Its \"byte-identical to `scripts/build.mjs`\" check can only hold for an uninstrumented copy built with `PRODUCTION` plus the plugin.\n\n### Step 4: exact duplicates\n- `setAttr`: one copy in new `dom/attributes.ts`, used by figure, toolbar, table and interaction. `table.ts`'s variant skipped the `hasAttribute` check; removing an absent attribute is a no-op, so behaviour is the same.\n- `clamp`: `lookup/aligned` now uses `scene/geometry`'s.\n- `withUnit`: `core/axes` now uses `reader/table`'s.\n- Binary search: `focus.lowerBound` and the controller's `indexOf` now use `lookup/search`.\n- Message-key allowlist: now `Object.keys(defaultMessages)`. I checked that it has the same 60 keys in the same order, which matters for suggestion ties.\n- `store-unaligned`'s `lowerBound` stays a commented copy, because `test/data/review.test.ts` forbids data importing lookup.\n\n### Final sizes (from the packed tarballs)\n| Case | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| everything | 107,960 (105.43 KiB) | 106,738 (104.24 KiB) |\n| line only (first-chart npm.ts) | 107,835 | 89,605 (87.50 KiB) |\n| line export | — | 89,516 |\n| area | ~107.6 KB | 91,514 |\n| bar | ~107.6 KB | 89,997 |\n| scatter | ~107.6 KB | 83,830 |\n| donut | ~107.6 KB | 77,125 |\n| validate | ~21 KB | 20,887 |\n| script tag (iife.min + css) | 110.53 KiB | 106,833 + 2,886 = 107.15 KiB |\n| React adapter | 1.63 KiB | 1.63 KiB |\n\nI restored `bench/size-latest.json` after each `size.mjs` run. Note that `scripts/size.mjs`'s per-module breakdown rebuilds without the stylesheet plugin, so it now wrongly prints \"dist was built from different source\". `size.mjs` was outside my files; it should use `stylesheetPlugin` and `PRODUCTION` from `build.mjs`.\n\n### Last lines of every suite\n- `npm run typecheck`: clean.\n- `npx vitest run`: `Tests 1 failed | 1579 passed (1580)`. The one failure is the known `streaming-storage` memory-budget test.\n- Browser, SVG, all of `packages/axylo/test/browser`: `Test Files 33 passed | 1 skipped (34)`, `Tests 834 passed | 1 skipped (835)`. Same result at step 1 and on the final build.\n- Browser, canvas, chart and a11y: `Tests 193 passed (193)`, at step 1 and on the final build.\n- Dist, Node: `Tests 1 failed | 116 passed (117)`. The failure is `conditions.test.ts > @axylo/react > production file carries none of the development-only text`. It is not mine: I confirmed in a temporary worktree of HEAD that it fails there too, and the React build is byte-identical to HEAD's. The cause is `patch.ts`'s `{ value }` shorthand, which appears as `value:` in the minified file.\n- Dist, browser: `Tests 8 failed | 22 passed (30)`. All 8 are `csp.browser.test.ts`, failing with \"axylo.css declares no light --axylo-default-series-1\". Also not mine: they fail identically at HEAD. The test's hex regex predates the `light-dark()` tokens added in e9449a6.\n- React: `Tests 39 passed (39)` at step 1 and on the final build.\n- `apps/docs` browser: `6 failed | 1 passed` files. **This one is caused by my change.** The docs guard in `apps/docs/lib/site.mjs` (`checkSameRevision`) requires the installed `axylo.css` to equal `css.ts`'s string. The exact fix: compare against `minifyCss(AXYLO_CSS)` from `src/theme/minify.ts`. `apps/docs/lib/theme.mjs`'s `block()` also expects `selector + ' {'` and a `;` after every declaration, so it needs to accept the minified form. I did not edit `apps/docs`. The docs agent is blocked by this until it is relayed. If you would rather keep `dist/axylo.css` readable instead, that is a one-line change in `build.mjs`.\n\n### Shared code that still names other kinds (kept on purpose, all small and with no module edges)\n- The `resolveOptions` key table, `readX`'s type checks, `viewStateFor`, `KIND_NAMES` / `KIND_MESSAGES`.\n- Inline frame-shape branches in the controller: `formatSpec` with `pointDateUnit`, `pointFor`, `freeze`, `latestX`, `renamed`, `positionValue`, `hasData`, `themeKeys`.\n- Inline branches in interaction: `aligned()` checks, `stepAcross` used for initial focus, the ring hole in placement.\n- Bar bands and the stack inside the aligned view, which all three aligned kinds share.\n\nThese are the next candidates if you want more off `line`, estimated at a few hundred bytes gzip.\n\n### Things that looked wrong (not fixed)\n- The `conditions` and CSP dist test failures above, both pre-existing.\n- `controller.ts` imports `fill`, which was already unused at HEAD.\n\n### What a reviewer should look at first\n1. `src/kinds/*`: is the set of mark handlers per kind complete (scene plus overlay marks)?\n2. `view/index.ts` `cartesianBase` and the `scene/index.ts` split: is the order of diagnostics and layers the same as before?\n3. The registry rewritten as data in `diagnostics/registry.ts`.\n4. The guard expression in `controller.ts` / `instrument.ts`.\n5. `theme/minify.ts` and the docs conflict above.\n\nAll of `packages/axylo/src`, `scripts/build.mjs`, `tests/dist/licence.test.ts`, `tests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts`, `packages/axylo/test/theme/minify.test.ts` and `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` are under `/home/canarit/projects/axylo`. The scratch directory has been removed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
