{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md && rg -n 'series 33|pattern|jump|touch|pinch|picker|minimum|readout|focus' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core{5,6}.fix.report.md | cut -c1-410\"","aggregated_output":"<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, seventh pass: report\n\nAll five items are done. Browser acceptance on SVG now passes in full, 555 of 555, and both items you asked me to confirm (I5 and L1 bar at 200% text) pass in it. Nothing is committed; I did not swap the shared `dist` (old-code checks used private builds of 4504ca4 via `AXYLO_BUNDLE`).\n\n### 1. Rule 3b: a rest holds the datum along the corridor (`src/dom/interaction.ts`)\n- **Rest:** a pointer that stays within 2 CSS px for 250 ms, measured with the events' own timestamps, has rested.\n- **Where it applies:** when the datum's floating tooltip is not across the reading axis (beside a bar or stack; always on scatter and donut).\n- **Hold:** after a rest, the datum is held while the pointer is inside the convex hull of the resting point and the tooltip's rectangle. Leaving the hull resumes picking on that same move; a pointer that never rested is never held. The tooltip stays pointer-transparent and does not move.\n- **One adjustment:** the corridor opens on the first move after the rest, even a move of 2 px or less. Without that, a datum resting exactly on a band edge (the acceptance bar probe) changed on the first 1 px step.\n- **Tests:** five browser tests in `test/browser/chart/review6.browser.test.ts`:\n  - bar after a rest;\n  - bar without a rest, where the datum changes;\n  - leaving the rectangle away from the corridor;\n  - a fast sweep after a rest elsewhere;\n  - donut with the tooltip in the hole.\n\n  On 4504ca4 the three that need the hold fail; the no-rest and sweep tests also pass on old code, so they only guard.\n\n### 2. L4 on a prefers-color-scheme change, fixed in CSS (`src/theme/`)\n- **Stylesheet (`css.ts`):** the `.axylo` private defaults are now `light-dark(light, dark)`, so they switch in the frame the media query does. Fixed sets remain under `[data-axylo-scheme=\"light\"]` and `[data-axylo-scheme=\"dark\"]`. The comment says `light-dark()` is supported by the current and previous major versions of the four browsers in spec 2.3.\n- **Resolution (`resolve.ts`):** when the chart's computed `color-scheme` is anything but `normal` and no `--axylo-background` decides, no `data-axylo-scheme` is written. The per-series properties were already references, not frozen colours.\n  - With `color-scheme: normal` or `--axylo-background`, it works as before.\n  - Forced colours and `prefers-contrast` are unchanged and still pass in the render suite.\n- **Canvas:** it still repaints when the change event arrives, one frame behind; a comment in `controller.ts` says so, and AX141 is judged then.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `test/theme/review.test.ts` checks the generated stylesheet.\n  - `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` emulates the media change under `color-scheme: light dark` and reads the mark colour in the first rAF. It fails on 4504ca4.\n- **Tests changed:** three render tests and two of my chart tests expected the attribute in \"page sets color-scheme\" cases. They now expect none, which is the design change, not a loosened check.\n\n### 3. Two-tone focus ring (palette review B1)\n- **Datum ring (`core/focus.ts`):** a 4 px background-colour surround with the 2 px focus colour on top, i.e. 1 px of background on each side. Corners are closed, the ring is kept inside the plot's box, and the tooltip's avoid-box grows by the surround (`RING_REACH` 10).\n- **Plot outline (`css.ts`):** an inset `box-shadow` in the background colour under the 2 px outline. `forced-color-adjust: none` keeps it in forced colours, where both tokens are already system colours.\n- **Tests:**\n  - New browser test (`review6`): dark scheme, a bar of each of the 8 dark series colours, painted pixels at device pixel ratio 2. Crossing the ring finds background, then focus colour, then background, and the ring really crosses the neighbouring bar. It fails on 4504ca4 and passes on both renderers.\n  - `test/core/focus.test.ts`: its expectation changed from 4 focus rules to 4 surround rules plus 4 focus rules.\n- The acceptance A2 tests still pass.\n\n### 4. Untitled chart named by its target's id (React review C6)\n- `Host.targetId`, from `root.id` in `chart.ts`, is used for the diagnostic chart name and for the internal-error delivery. The allocated id stays for the DOM relationships.\n- Node tests in `snapshot.test.ts`: \"sessions\" when the target has that id, the allocated id otherwise. `test/core/host.ts` has a new `targetId` option.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- `src/theme/css.ts`: the token blocks and the ring surround.\n- `src/theme/resolve.ts`: the scheme attribute rule only.\n- `test/theme/review.test.ts`, `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` (new), and the expectations in `test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts` and `review.browser.test.ts`.\n- `test/browser/chart/util.ts`: `AXYLO_BUNDLE` now also reaches the render suites, without the renderer switch.\n- `palette.ts` and `test/theme/palette.test.ts` show as modified in the tree, but those are the palette author's changes, not mine.\n\n### Runs (last lines, final build)\n- **Type check:** clean.\n  - In the chained run it failed once with `packages/react/src/index.ts(114,50): error TS2554`, while the React author was editing that file.\n  - Re-run afterwards: `tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit && tsc -p docs/api && tsc -p packages/react && tsc -p tests/dist`, no errors.\n- **Node suite without acceptance:** `Test Files 2 failed | 44 passed (46)`, `Tests 2 failed | 791 passed (793)`. Neither failure is mine:\n  - the kept memory test (`data/streaming-storage`);\n  - `scene/scene.test.ts` \"keeps generated geometry finite and clipped across independent chart states\", which fails identically on a clean HEAD tree (2727a30).\n- **My browser directories, SVG:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n- **My browser directories, canvas:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n- **Render (browser):** `Test Files 6 passed | 1 skipped (7)`, `Tests 86 passed | 1 skipped (87)`.\n- **Theme (Node):** `Test Files 3 passed (3)`, `Tests 52 passed (52)`.\n- **Browser acceptance, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 555 passed (555)`.\n\nLogs are `s3-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:18:- **`src/core/controller.ts`, readout mode by layout.** The plot rectangle without the strip, laid out in the plot's whole column (`room`, from `chart.ts` `measure()`), is under 240 × 140. One more condition: the plot must keep the L8 minimum of 80 px beside the strip.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:22:- **Figure and CSS:** the readout element now sits in the plot's column under the plot (`figure.ts`). The strip is two reserved lines (`css.ts`, figure section).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:23:- **Rings are drawn inside the plot's box** (`core/focus.ts` `buildOverlay`), so the ring at the last point and at the top of a donut is painted. The A2 focus-indicator tests pass.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:33:  - The donut focus outline uses `donutGeometry`'s adjusted angles.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:36:- **Item 6:** `focus.ts` takes the total from the lookup's tooltip model and computes no net total.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:39:1. **I1 \"readout mode … 139 px high\", 5 types.** Entering readout mode reserves the strip, so the plot jumps from about 140 px straight to about 92 px; no plot height exists in between. The test's bisection (`plotTo`) stops on whichever side it probed last, and here it is the 140.07 px side. At 139 px the library is in readout mode. The width bracket passes.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:56:  - The narrow-tile and axe readout tests use a 220 px tile, since readout mode now starts below 240 px.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:57:  - The readout text may end in \"+N more\".\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core6.fix.report.md:63:- **No layout changes.** I tried a `minimum` option in `src/layout` during the pass, then removed it, and `src/layout` and `test/layout` match HEAD. The final full run happened before that removal, with the option present but unused.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:5:Nothing is committed and the tree compiles. Everything you listed is done except interaction item 13 with decision 0004 rule 4 (the readout's reserved space) and part of the part-3 weak-test list; both are explained under \"Not done\". I did not touch the shared `dist` to test old code: the old revision (88a8b96) is built privately at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-ca\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:9:- **Fix:** each tick set is now checked on its own tick values. The first tick at or above the maximum must be the last tick, and the last tick at or below the minimum must be the first. `scale/domain.ts` was already exact.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:17:- Values on a percent or ratio scale keep their F6 readout digits.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:20:### C4: the series colour on the pattern overlay\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:21:- `render/svg.ts` `updateBars`: the overlay rects that carry the pattern also carry the series colour style. The colour is part of the cache key, so a theme change updates it.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:22:- Test in `test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts`: the elements carrying the series colour whose fill is a pattern. It failed before the fix and passes now; the render suite is 84 passed, 1 skipped.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:27:| new 9 | Choosable tooltip rows and every donut slice-list entry (zero and null slices included) are buttons named by their text, with `tabindex=-1`, so the closed chart still has two tab stops. Clicking a slice entry selects it; the press does not move focus. Opening the table by keyboard closes a pin (this already worked). | 2 of 3 tests fail on old; the \nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:29:| part 1 item 9 | `minimumWidth` is now at most half the axis and at least one unit in the last place: two or three positions over [0,100] can be halved, and [1e16, 1e16+4] halves to a width of 2. | Node tests in `focus2.test.ts` failed before the fix |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:31:| part 1 item 12 | `core/chart.ts` `measure()` now gives layout pixels rather than transformed viewport pixels. One conversion (`cssScale` in `tooltip.ts`) is used for picking, anchors, tooltip size and placement, and the readout. Ratios within 2% are treated as offsetWidth's integer rounding, not as a transform. | fails on old |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:38:- With 24 px rows everywhere, the hover tooltip grew about 12 px. At two plot edges it then no longer fit beside the mark, so the existing test \"at each of the four plot edges…\" fell back to the readout and failed.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:39:- What I did: rows are 24 px when the tooltip is pinned by a tap, in the fixed readout, and in the slice list. A mouse-hover tooltip keeps text-height rows, which are still buttons.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:40:- So WCAG 2.5.8 is met wherever rows are acted on by touch. It is not met for mouse clicks on hover rows. If you want 24 px rows there too, tell me and I will change the edge test's fixture instead.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:47:- Coarse-double loop in `focus2` (pass 4).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:49:Expectations I changed because the requirement changed: \"two or three positions cannot be zoomed\" (focus2 and review2) became the attainable-minimum rule; \"the legend has no buttons\" became buttons outside the tab order; the note runs in `snapshot.test.ts` are now per run.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:59:`focus.ts` already takes the total text from the lookup's tooltip model and computes no net. A Node test checks a stack of +3 and −2: the tooltip total is \"3 and -2\" and the focused text contains \"Total 3 and -2\".\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:70:- **Item 13 with rule 4 (reserved space for the readout).** Reserving space when the floating tooltip might not fit costs a small tile's plot room on every chart; that is why I reverted it in pass 3. Placing the readout inside the plot column stops it covering the controls but drops \"reserved\". I need a decision: reserve space only below some figure width (w\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:75:  - selecting a secondary row by touch in the readout (the pinned-tooltip case is covered);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
