lso, the reported 25% closing-pair minima of **0.029276** light and **0.036923** dark describe normal vision. Across all four visions, slot\n47:The stated dark costs reproduce. Purple is **3.07393:1** and the first blue is **6.3476:1**, down from **3.2621:1** and **7.4615:1** in the superseded palette. The nearest dark series to focus, reference and muted are **green 0.104214**, **green 0.107272** and **pink 0.102348**. In light they are **cyan 0.115745**, **green 0.121400** and **cyan 0.111079**. The old dark focus `#79a8ff` is **0.050095** from B’s blue. The earlier report’s **0.024** applies to the superseded blue. Light red and purple rose from chromas **0.13026 / 0.20512** to **0.19998 / 0.21955**. [Decision costs](</home/canarit/projec\n51:I composited in encoded sRGB over each scheme background. Each cell gives **ideal / rounded-alpha bytes / floored-alpha bytes**. At 80%, both byte models use alpha 204 and give identical results, so those rows show **ideal / bytes**.\n55:| Light 25% | .0798/.0802/.0790 | .0687/.0687/.0674 | .0800/.0799/.0788 | .0645/.0641/.0636 | .0881/.0885/.0880 | .0771/.0765/.0762 | .0827/.0822/.0821 |\n56:| Dark 25% | .0947/.0940/.0936 | .0854/.0843/.0850 | .1304/.1296/.1267 | .0684/.0673/.0694 | .1159/.1150/.1146 | .0671/.0675/.0664 | .0639/.0638/.0641 |\n57:| Light 80% | .2518/.2514 | .2229/.2237 | .2604/.2606 | .2340/.2344 | .2807/.2801 | .2415/.2413 | .2578/.2573 |\n58:| Dark 80% | .2519/.2515 | .2247/.2244 | .3512/.3512 | .1811/.1810 | .3044/.3043 | .1747/.1744 | .1820/.1812 |\n60:| Minimum | Light 25% | Dark 25% | Light 80% | Dark 80% |\n78:| 1 · Opaque contrast | Yes, below 3:1 in the affected scheme. |\n111:The contrast column also gives the **background-coloured surround against each opaque mark**. Neighbours are other slot numbers in the same scheme. The worst distance is the analytic minimum over all four visions. P, D and T denote protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. Token distances are in focus / reference / muted order.