series are AX108 and that series is not drawn. On scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data. | Shuffled `trend` renders identically; duplicate fixture | R5 |\n111:| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to at most three lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In real browsers, after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2 |\n124:| I1 | Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the picking rule for the chart type (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row at that x reads \"No observation\", distinct from \"No data\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, does not cover the active mark or any control, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \"+N more\". In a plot too small for it (decision 0004: narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px) the same content appears as text in a strip reserved under the plot. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum. | Hover at 20 positions including all four edges; sparse-series fixture; narrow tile with eight series; Escape test | R15 |\n137:| A1 | Every chart has an accessible name: its `title`, or the heading named by `labelledBy`, or else a generated name (\"Line chart of Sessions by Day\") with AX140 raised in every build. The title's heading level is the author's (`level`), and it can be hidden visually. Every chart has a generated summary: type, series, x range with time zone, y range, each series' minimum, maximum and last value, and any omissions. `description` adds to the summary and never removes the zone or omission statements. Element ids are unique per chart. | Accessibility-tree snapshot for every fixture; a 24-chart page has no duplicate ids; axe `heading-order` | R11, R13 |\n141:| A5 | Series are never distinguished by color alone, in any mode. Each line and area carries a shape marker at its last point and at sparse intervals, repeated in the legend and tooltip; under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors, lines also differ by dash. Adjacent filled marks (slices, stacked segments) are separated by at least 1 px of background. The default palette has eight colors, each at least 3:1 on the default light and dark backgrounds, with a minimum pairwise OKLab difference of 0.10 (provisional) under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. On any other background, Axylo measures the palette against the resolved background and raises AX141 below 3:1. | Palette script scoring the rendered marks of an eight-series chart in both schemes, repeats included; rendered-pixel checks of separators; a grayscale screenshot in which three crossing lines can be told apart by marker | R7, WCAG 1.4.1, 1.4.11 |\n142:| A6 | Content reflows at 320 CSS px and 400% zoom without two-dimensional scrolling. User text-spacing overrides do not clip text. | Viewport and style-override tests in three engines | WCAG 1.4.10, 1.4.12 |\n159:| AX105 | Hint | Steps are absent on a regular time, date, wall-clock or number axis | Gaps. When a series would need more absent steps than twice its observations (and more than 1,000), it is treated as irregular instead: no gaps are created and the hint says so |\n206:| C1 | A compact chart is a static image with a full text alternative: `role=\"img\"`, an accessible name (as in A1, including AX140 when none is given) and the generated summary as its description (series, x range, minimum, maximum, last value, omissions). It has no tab stop and no pointer-only behavior, so nothing is available to a mouse that is not available to a keyboard. | Accessibility-tree snapshot; a page of 40 has zero added tab stops |\n   194\t        // When the plot is squeezed to nothing, how far the rest overflows the figure is how much room is\n   198\t        return { width: plot.width / sx, height: plot.height / sy - overflow, room: { width: stage.width / sx, height: stage.height / sy } };\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^[0-9]+'\"\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core2.review.md | cut -c1-460 && sed -n '644,704p;1348,1374p' packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts && sed -n '1,55p' packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review3.browser.test.ts\"","aggregated_output":"7:1. **B · Paused appends violate call order and synchronous validation. Reasoned.** Pause a scatter chart, append A, replace the data with B, zoom, then resume. A is replayed against B using the later options and zoom. On a strict chart, an invalid paused append returns successfully. Resume catches the eventual exception, logs it, and discards the remaining queued batches, including valid ones. On aligned charts, even a *rejected* replacement can clear `h\n9:2. **B · Category eviction changes the identity of keyboard focus. Ran the store and lookup. Reasoned through the slider and selection event.** With categories `A, B, C`, I focused B at ordinal 1 and appended D with `keep: 3`. The new frame contained `B, C, D` in the same epoch. Resolving the saved reference returned **C**, value 2, source row 2. Since the reference still compares equal, the focused slider can continue to say **B** while Enter selects **\n11:3. **B · An empty zoom removes its own Reset control. Ran the view and zoom arithmetic. Reasoned through control removal.** On a numeric line with observations at `0,1,3,4,96,98,99,100`, one centered zoom produced `[25,75]` with zero value slots. The resulting empty state hides the proxy and removes Zoom out and Reset. Neither `0` nor a click can recover the original view. This makes the controller review’s empty-window finding worse. The same `ready` g\n13:4. **B · A focused slider freezes its native bounds as well as its text. Reasoned.** Focus a one-point chart, then append a second point. The reference and mode compare equal, so `writeProxy` returns before updating `max`, `value`, or `aria-valuetext`. A touch-reader increment encounters the old maximum of zero and can produce no `input` event. A physical arrow key happens to repair the bounds in `syncNative`. The same shortcut leaves an obsolete ordina\n17:5. **M · `keep` does not bound retained memory. Ran the aligned store. Reasoned through controller ownership.** After 1,000 appends with `keep: 3`, the frame held 3 rows and the store reported **1,001 retained rows**. Retiring superseded revisions reduced retention to 3. The controller never calls `retire`. Paused scatter and donut charts additionally keep a copy of every incoming batch until Resume, even with `keep: 1`. Retain the displayed snapshot an\n19:6. **M · A clamped key can reverse the next assistive action. Reasoned.** Press Home at ordinal 0. The handler saves `intent = 'first'`, but the native value does not change, so no `input` clears it. An assistive increment to 1 then consumes the stale Home and returns to 0. Held keys at an endpoint have the same problem. A direct assistive value-set from 10 to 70 is interpreted as one page; a `change`-only notification has no handler. Also, tabbing onto\n21:7. **M · Keyboard exploration drops information available to the pointer. Ran.** With A at x=0 and 2 and hidden B at x=1, lookup counted three slots and the pointer reported “No observation” at 1. Right jumped directly from 0 to 2. For coincident scatter points, the pointer target contained two refs while the keyboard-created target contained one. On alternating scatter series, switching from A to B and pressing Right landed back on A. For a stacked are\n23:8. **M · Panning and selection lack single-pointer equivalents. Reasoned.** Zoom in, then try to move the window right using taps or clicks alone. The toolbar only scales around the center or resets. Shift+Right, a drag, or a two-finger gesture can reach ranges that the buttons cannot. A mouse click and Enter/Space emit `select`; a touch tap only pins. A fresh mouse user also cannot explicitly select a secondary aligned series at the same x as the prima\n25:9. **M · Enabled zoom controls can do nothing or produce a zero-width window. Ran.** For `[0,100]` with two or three aligned x positions, the computed minimum width was 200 or 100. Zoom in returned `null` at full view. Drag accepts half that minimum, so one input method can reach a range another cannot. On scatter `[10¹⁶,10¹⁶+4]`, the second halving produced two identical endpoints. The focused wheel calls `preventDefault()` even when zoom cannot move. \n27:10. **M · Gesture cancellation and pinch anchoring are inconsistent. Reasoned; ran the horizontal projection arithmetic.** Start a captured drag and press Escape. The document handler clears `down` without releasing capture or consuming the active cancellation, so a containing dialog can close too. There is no lost-capture or window-blur cleanup. A second non-touch pointer overwrites the drag, and a remaining pinch finger can be treated as a fresh tap a\n29:11. **M · A pinned scatter tooltip survives removal of its marks. Ran the lookup distinction. Reasoned through commit.** Tap to pin a scatter point, then programmatically zoom it out of view. Commit keeps the old target if `lookup.tooltip(oldTarget)` returns any rows. That lookup can format a source row outside the current view. I also obtained two tooltip rows for two previously coincident points after hiding both series in a new lookup. Validate pinne\n31:12. **M · Tooltip positioning can cover a mark, escape the viewport, or be clipped. Reasoned.** Hover a chart under `transform: scale(2)`. Pointer deltas are viewport pixels passed to a layout-pixel lookup, and the tooltip translation mixes viewport bounds with unscaled `offsetWidth` and `offsetHeight`. In an overflow-clipped card, a candidate can fit the viewport but extend beyond the card. When no candidate fits, the last branch still shows a clamped \n33:13. **M · The narrow readout covers the controls and disappears when approached. Reasoned.** In the 260 px tile, hover a point and move onto the readout. `pointerleave` exempts only the floating tooltip, so the readout disappears. When touch-pinned, the opaque readout sits directly over the toolbar at `z-index: 3`; tapping it counts as inside and cannot activate the button underneath. Keyboard dismissal also persists too long: dismiss at A, move to B, t\n35:14. **M · Keyboard focus can be entirely invisible on a donut. Ran the overlay and layout. Reasoned about clipping.** Tab to a donut whose first slice has value zero and whose second slice is positive. In a 320×200 layout, the plot occupied `(0,0,320,200)`. The first slice had no anchor and produced no overlay. The remaining CSS focus outline is drawn outside that exact rectangle and clipped by the plot’s `overflow: hidden`; the native input is transpar\n37:15. **M · Opening the table overflows fixed cards and moves auto-height neighbors. Reasoned.** Open a table in a short fixed-height card. The code freezes the plot at its former pixel height, then inserts the table and pager below the controls. A clipping card hides them; an unclipped card can cover the next chart. In an auto-height stack, following charts move. A 100 px plot can also receive a 160 px scroll region because of `Math.max(160, height)`. Th\n39:16. **M · An open table announces incoming data. Reasoned.** Leave page 1 open with 200 rows and append row 201. Rendering changes the polite region from “Page 1 of 2” to “Page 1 of 3” without reader action. Page clamping after eviction can do the same. The 24-stream test opens no tables and observes only live regions present at setup. Keep the visible count current and announce page changes only from reader-initiated paging or jumping. **A7, WCAG 4.1.3\n41:17. **M · One `tabindex=\"0\"` does not guarantee that focus survives a render. Reasoned.** Focus legend B, then update wide fields from `[A,B]` to `[B,A]`. The renderer moves B using `insertBefore`; ordinary removal and reinsertion can drop focus. Its restoration path runs only when the key disappears. With focus in the jump field, disabling the table removes the active element without a handoff. Shrinking to one page likewise hides the focused pager. Pr\n43:18. **M · “Jump to” can reject the displayed x or jump to another one. Ran the table model. Reasoned through the field.** The model accepted canonical ISO dates and instants, but rejected its own displayed `May 31, 2026` and `May 31, 2026, 12:00 AM UTC`. The field also rejects the displayed English `900,000`, while removing all whitespace turns `1 2` into 12. Its parser captures the x kind when the table opens, so changing a numeric axis to categories c\n45:19. **M · The plot ignores translation keys and exposes English under the page language. Ran the value formatter. Reasoned through language inheritance.** Overrides for `pointAll`, `seriesValue`, and `position` still produced `0: a 2; b 3. Point 1 of 2.` The role description uses `typeLine` directly instead of `plotRole`. On a German page, the default slider label, role description, value text, generated summary, and polite state announcement can all in\n47:20. **M · An axis can retain the wrong unit after an update. Ran.** I built a wide line with A and B both in `ms`, then changed only B to `s`. The production view and layout-input paths produced `Value (ms)` and `Value`, respectively, but `sameKey` returned `true`. The controller can therefore keep a milliseconds axis title while the tooltip and table use the new units. Include the effective axis title and shared unit in the layout key. **L6, plan 1.5.*\n49:21. **M · The accessibility tests cannot establish several claimed outcomes. Reasoned from the tests.** `axNode` gets role, name, value, and maximum from Chrome, but gets its decisive spoken-text assertion directly from `getAttribute('aria-valuetext')`. The focus-obscuration assertion compares areas; a small tooltip can pass while completely covering the focused mark. The axe helper scans `body` with default rules and no explicit rule exclusions, but co\n53:22. **m · High-contrast line swatches do not repeat the plotted dash. Reasoned.** Enable forced colors or increased contrast on a multi-line chart. The plotted lines switch to their contrast dash, while legend and tooltip swatches read only `cue.dash.normal`. Marker shapes still provide a cue, but the legend can show a solid sample for a dashed line. Bind swatches to the same normal and contrast patterns as the marks and inspect both at eight and more t\n        frameRevision = Math.max(frameRevision, prepared.frame.revision);\n        commitAppend = null;\n        const check = new DiagnosticCollector();\n        const resolved = store.resolveEncoding(publicOptions(previous.options), check);\n        if (!check.inputs().some(d => d.code === 'AX101')) {\n          const again: PreparedFrame<Frame> = store.prepareReencode(resolved, nextVersion());\n          commitAppend = again.commit;\n          c = {\n            ...c, resolved, source: resolved, frame: again.frame, dataDiagnostics: again.diagnostics, dataOptions: [],\n            optionDiagnostics: previous.optionDiagnostics.filter(d => !DATA_CODES.has(d.code)),\n          };\n        }\n      }\n      const viewed = viewFor(c, base);\n      const found = [...prepared.callDiagnostics, ...viewed.found];\n      rejectIfStrict(previous.options.strict === true, found, previous.name, previous.options.onDiagnostic);\n      if (paused) {\n        prepared.commit();\n        storeFrames.add(prepared.frame);\n        frameRevision = Math.max(frameRevision, prepared.frame.revision);\n        // The store is the accepted state's now; rows no displayed or pending frame needs go (finding 4).\n        accepted = { ...previous, store };\n        release();\n        // The held state: complete findings for the data accepted so far, kept apart from what is drawn, so a\n        // display effect (an error state) never reaches the ring on screen before Resume (finding 6).\n        held = { frame: prepared.frame, dataDiagnostics: prepared.diagnostics, viewDiagnostics: viewed.viewDiagnostics };\n        streaming = true;\n        deliverChanges();\n        schedule();\n        return;\n      }\n      streaming = true;\n      accept(c, viewed, previous.follow && zoom !== null, commitAppend);\n    });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The caller's rows of a displayed frame as a table, in source order and with their own source indexes, so\n   * they can be normalized again on their own (re-encoding what is on screen while paused).\n   */\n  function displayedTable(frame: Frame): Table {\n    const own = onScreen && onScreen.frame === frame && onScreen.frozen ? onScreen.frozen : freeze(frame).rows;\n    const indexes = [...own.keys()].sort((p, q) => p - q);\n    const rows = indexes.map(i => own.get(i));\n    // Positions read the rows in order; provenance and events read them by their own source index.\n    return { ...rowsTable(rows), rowIndex: i => indexes[i]!, rowAt: index => own.get(index) ?? null };\n  }\n\n  /** The caller's rows every slot of `frame` refers to, read once, so the frame stays addressable on its own. */\n  function freeze(frame: Frame): { frame: Frame; rows: Map<number, unknown> } {\n    const rows = new Map<number, unknown>();\n    const keep = (row: number) => { if (row >= 0 && !rows.has(row)) rows.set(row, frame.source.rowAt(row)); };\n    const each = (index: Int32Array | null, length: number) => {\n      for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) keep(index ? index[i]! : i);\n    };\n    if (frame.shape === 'aligned') for (const s of frame.series) each(s.row, frame.length);\n    else if (frame.shape === 'points') for (const s of frame.series) each(s.row, s.x.length);\n    else each(frame.row, frame.labels.length);\n    return { frame, rows };\n  }\n\n   * only retire \"everything up to a revision\", so a displayed frame older than revisions that were accepted\n   * since takes a copy of its rows once the store has grown past twice its last size), and a pending frame\n   * that has not been drawn yet keeps its own. Runs after every accepted call and every published frame,\n   * whether or not frames run (review 3, controller blockers 2 and 4).\n   */\n  function release(): void {\n    const store = accepted?.store;\n    if (!store) return;\n    const needed: Frame[] = [];\n    const shown = onScreen && onScreen.store === store && !onScreen.frozen && storeFrames.has(onScreen.frame) ? onScreen : null;\n    if (shown) needed.push(shown.frame);\n    const pending = accepted!.frame;\n    if (storeFrames.has(pending) && pending !== store.frame && pending !== onScreen?.frame) needed.push(pending);\n    if (shown && store.retainedRowCount > 2 * retainedBaseline + 64) {\n      shown.frozen = freeze(shown.frame).rows;\n      needed.splice(needed.indexOf(shown.frame), 1);\n    }\n    const floor = needed.length ? Math.min(...needed.map(f => f.revision)) : store.frame.revision;\n    if (floor > 0) store.retire(floor - 1);\n  }\n\n  /** The displayed snapshot is now `frame` (or nothing): its rows are owned until the next one is drawn. */\n  function showing(a: Accepted | null): void {\n    const frame = a?.frame ?? null;\n    onScreen = frame === null ? null : { frame, store: a!.store, frozen: onScreen?.frame === frame ? onScreen.frozen : null };\n    release();\n    retainedBaseline = accepted?.store?.retainedRowCount ?? 0;\n/**\n * The third reviews (reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.controller.review.md and core3.interaction.review.md),\n * as seen from the page. Node sequences of the controller review are in test/core/snapshot.test.ts.\n */\nimport { afterAll, beforeAll, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport type { Page } from 'playwright-core';\nimport { start, stop } from '../harness';\nimport { chartPage, closePage } from './util';\n\nbeforeAll(start);\nafterAll(stop);\n\nconst valueText = (page: Page) => page.locator('#chart .axylo-proxy').getAttribute('aria-valuetext');\nconst settle = (page: Page) => page.evaluate(async () => { for (const c of window.charts) await c.__bench.ready(); await window.nextFrames(2); });\nconst button = (page: Page, text: string) => page.locator('#chart button', { hasText: text });\n\nasync function create(page: Page, kind: string, options: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {\n  await page.evaluate(async ({ kind, options }) => {\n    const chart = window.Axylo[kind]!('#chart', options);\n    window.charts.push(chart);\n    await chart.__bench.ready();\n    await window.nextFrames(1);\n  }, { kind, options });\n}\n\ndescribe('interaction blocker 1: an assistive value change always ends', () => {\n  it('scatter A0 B1 A2 B3 A4, narrowed to B, set to 2: lands on A2 at once', async () => {\n    const page = await chartPage();\n    const data = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map(x => ({ x, s: x % 2 ? 'B' : 'A', y: x }));\n    await create(page, 'scatter', { title: 'S', data, x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 's' });\n    await page.focus('#chart .axylo-proxy');\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\n    expect(await valueText(page)).toMatch(/^B,/);\n    const done = await Promise.race([\n      page.evaluate(() => {\n        const proxy = document.querySelector('#chart .axylo-proxy') as HTMLInputElement;\n        proxy.value = '2';\n        proxy.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\n        return 'ended';\n      }),\n      new Promise<string>(r => setTimeout(() => r('hung'), 5000)),\n    ]);\n    expect(done).toBe('ended');\n    expect(await valueText(page)).toMatch(/Point 3 of 5/);\n    expect(await valueText(page)).toMatch(/^A,/);\n    expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('interaction blocker 2: the open table covers the plot, never its controls', () => {\n  it(\"with legend: 'right' the Hide table button stays visible and hittable, and focus moves into the table\", async () => {\n    const page = await chartPage();\n    const data = [0, 1, 2].flatMap(x => ['a', 'b'].map(s => ({ x, s, y: x })));\n    await create(page, 'line', { title: 'R', data, x: 'x', y: 'y', series: 's', legend: 'right' });\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show a518cbb:packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts | nl -ba | sed -n '135,260p;413,487p;718,766p' && nl -ba packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter.ts | sed -n '87,223p'\"","aggregated_output":"   135\t    it(`I1 ${type}: at 20 positions, the four edges included, what is there is shown by the type's picking rule within one frame of the move (95th percentile, counted in animation frames), inside the viewport, without covering the active mark`, async () => {\n   136\t      const page = await devPage({ css: 'body { margin: 0; } #chart { width: 100vw; height: 100vh; }' });\n   137\t      await create(page, type);\n   138\t      await frameClock(page);\n   139\t      const viewport = page.viewportSize()!;\n   140\t      const failures: string[] = [];\n   141\t      const latency: number[] = [];\n   142\t      const all = await probes(page, type);\n   143\t      for (const probe of all) {\n   144\t        if (!probe.marks.length) { failures.push(`${probe.x},${probe.y}: no active mark located`); continue; }\n   145\t        // From outside the chart each time, so the last tooltip is not what the pointer lands on.\n   146\t        await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n   147\t        await settle(page);\n   148\t        await page.mouse.move(probe.x, probe.y);\n   149\t        await settle(page);\n   150\t        const clock = await page.evaluate(() => (window as unknown as { clock: { moved: number; shown: number } }).clock);\n   151\t        latency.push(clock.shown < 0 ? Infinity : clock.shown - clock.moved);\n   152\t        // The tooltip, or where it cannot fit, the fixed readout under the plot (spec I1).\n   153\t        const surface = (await tooltip(page).isVisible()) ? '#chart .axylo-tooltip' : (await page.locator('#chart .axylo-readout').isVisible()) ? '#chart .axylo-readout' : null;\n   154\t        if (!surface) { failures.push(`${probe.x},${probe.y}: no tooltip and no readout`); continue; }\n   155\t        const text = (await page.locator(surface).textContent()) ?? '';\n   156\t        if (!says(text, probe)) failures.push(`${probe.x},${probe.y}: \"${text}\" lacks ${JSON.stringify(probe.expect)}`);\n   157\t        const t = await box(page, surface);\n   158\t        if (t.x < 0 || t.y < 0 || t.x + t.width > viewport.width || t.y + t.height > viewport.height) failures.push(`${probe.x},${probe.y}: outside the viewport`);\n   159\t        for (const m of covered(t, probe.marks)) failures.push(`${probe.x},${probe.y}: covers the active mark at ${Math.round(m.x)},${Math.round(m.y)}`);\n   160\t      }\n   161\t      expect(failures).toEqual([]);\n   162\t      const sorted = [...latency].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n   163\t      expect(sorted[Math.ceil(0.95 * sorted.length) - 1], `frames from move to readout: ${latency.join(', ')}`).toBeLessThanOrEqual(1);\n   164\t      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n   165\t    });\n   166\t\n   167\t    it(`I1 ${type}: the tooltip can itself be hovered (decision 0004 revision 2, rule 3b): after a 300 ms rest on the datum, moving straight onto the tooltip's rectangle, it stays for the same datum (same rows) and does not move at every step; with the pointer inside it, it is still shown; Escape closes it until another datum`, async () => {\n   168\t      const page = await devPage();\n   169\t      await create(page, type);\n   170\t      const all = await probes(page, type);\n   171\t      const first = all[type === 'donut' ? 2 : type === 'scatter' ? 4 : 10]!;\n   172\t      const other = all.find(p => p.expect[0] !== first.expect[0])!;\n   173\t      await page.mouse.move(first.x, first.y);\n   174\t      await settle(page);\n   175\t      expect(await tooltip(page).isVisible()).toBe(true);\n   176\t      const rows = () => page.locator('#chart .axylo-tooltip .axylo-tooltip-row').allTextContents();\n   177\t      const startRows = await rows();\n   178\t      expect(says(startRows.join(' ') + ((await page.locator('#chart .axylo-tooltip .axylo-tooltip-title').textContent()) ?? ''), first) || says((await tooltip(page).textContent()) ?? '', first)).toBe(true);\n   179\t      const startBox = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-tooltip');\n   180\t      // Rest 300 ms on the datum (decision 0004 rule 3b: a rest of 250 ms holds the datum along the corridor to\n   181\t      // a tooltip that is not across the reading axis; harmless where it is). Then straight onto the rectangle,\n   182\t      // to its point nearest the datum, 2 px inside, in 24 steps, every one checked from the first.\n   183\t      await page.waitForTimeout(300);\n   184\t      const target = { x: Math.min(startBox.x + startBox.width - 2, Math.max(startBox.x + 2, first.x)), y: Math.min(startBox.y + startBox.height - 2, Math.max(startBox.y + 2, first.y)) };\n   185\t      const failures: string[] = [];\n   186\t      for (let k = 1; k <= 24; k++) {\n   187\t        await page.mouse.move(first.x + ((target.x - first.x) * k) / 24, first.y + ((target.y - first.y) * k) / 24);\n   188\t        await settle(page);\n   189\t        if (!(await tooltip(page).isVisible())) { failures.push(`step ${k}: the tooltip closed`); break; }\n   190\t        const now = await rows();\n   191\t        if (JSON.stringify(now) !== JSON.stringify(startRows)) { failures.push(`step ${k}: rows changed to ${JSON.stringify(now)}`); break; }\n   192\t        const b = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-tooltip');\n   193\t        if (Math.abs(b.x - startBox.x) > 0.5 || Math.abs(b.y - startBox.y) > 0.5 || Math.abs(b.width - startBox.width) > 0.5 || Math.abs(b.height - startBox.height) > 0.5) { failures.push(`step ${k}: the tooltip moved from ${JSON.stringify(startBox)} to ${JSON.stringify(b)}`); break; }\n   194\t      }\n   195\t      expect(failures).toEqual([]);\n   196\t      const end = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-tooltip');\n   197\t      expect(inside({ ...target, width: 0, height: 0 }, end, 0), 'the pointer is inside the tooltip\\'s rectangle').toBe(true);\n   198\t      await page.keyboard.press('Escape');\n   199\t      await settle(page);\n   200\t      expect(await tooltip(page).isVisible()).toBe(false);\n   201\t      await page.mouse.move(first.x, first.y);\n   202\t      await settle(page);\n   203\t      expect(await tooltip(page).isVisible()).toBe(false);\n   204\t      await page.mouse.move(other.x, other.y);\n   205\t      await settle(page);\n   206\t      expect(await tooltip(page).isVisible()).toBe(true);\n   207\t      expect(says((await tooltip(page).textContent()) ?? '', other)).toBe(true);\n   208\t      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n   209\t    });\n   210\t\n   211\t    it(`I1 ${type}: a hovered tooltip is text, not controls (no button in Chrome's tree); a click on the plot pins it for that datum, its rows become buttons of at least 24 × 24 CSS px that select their series, and Escape dismisses it`, async () => {\n   212\t      const page = await devPage();\n   213\t      await create(page, type);\n   214\t      await page.evaluate(() => {\n   215\t        const w = window as unknown as { selected: string[]; charts: { on(e: string, f: (p: unknown) => void): void }[] };\n   216\t        w.selected = [];\n   217\t        w.charts[0]!.on('select', p => w.selected.push((p as { series: string }).series));\n   218\t      });\n   219\t      const probe = (await probes(page, type))[type === 'donut' ? 2 : type === 'scatter' ? 4 : 10]!;\n   220\t      await page.mouse.move(probe.x, probe.y);\n   221\t      await settle(page);\n   222\t      const buttonsIn = async () => (await axWithin(page, '#chart .axylo-tooltip').catch(() => [])).filter(n => n.role === 'button');\n   223\t      expect(await buttonsIn(), 'a hovered tooltip holds no buttons').toEqual([]);\n   224\t      await page.mouse.down();\n   225\t      await page.mouse.up();\n   226\t      await settle(page);\n   227\t      const pinned = page.locator('#chart .axylo-tooltip button, #chart .axylo-tooltip [role=\"button\"]');\n   228\t      const n = await pinned.count();\n   229\t      expect(n, 'the pinned tooltip has a button per row').toBeGreaterThan(0);\n   230\t      const small: string[] = [];\n   231\t      for (const b of await pinned.all()) { const r = (await b.boundingBox())!; if (r.width < 24 || r.height < 24) small.push(`${await b.textContent()}: ${r.width.toFixed(1)}×${r.height.toFixed(1)}`); }\n   232\t      expect(small).toEqual([]);\n   233\t      const before = await page.evaluate(() => (window as unknown as { selected: string[] }).selected.length);\n   234\t      const last = pinned.nth(n - 1);\n   235\t      const name = ((await last.textContent()) ?? '').trim();\n   236\t      await last.click();\n   237\t      await settle(page);\n   238\t      const selected = await page.evaluate(() => (window as unknown as { selected: string[] }).selected);\n   239\t      expect(selected.length).toBe(before + 1);\n   240\t      expect(name.startsWith(selected.at(-1)!), `\"${name}\" selects \"${selected.at(-1)}\"`).toBe(true);\n   241\t      await page.keyboard.press('Escape');\n   242\t      await settle(page);\n   243\t      expect(await tooltip(page).isVisible()).toBe(false);\n   244\t      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n   245\t    });\n   246\t\n   247\t    if (type !== 'scatter' && type !== 'donut') {\n   248\t      it(`I1 ${type}: a hovered tooltip never stalls picking: a fast sweep along the reading axis through the tooltip's rectangle shows a new datum at every step, and a click with the pointer over the tooltip selects the datum under the pointer`, async () => {\n   249\t        const page = await devPage();\n   250\t        await create(page, type);\n   251\t        await page.evaluate(() => {\n   252\t          const w = window as unknown as { picked: unknown[]; charts: { on(e: string, f: (p: unknown) => void): void }[] };\n   253\t          w.picked = [];\n   254\t          w.charts[0]!.on('select', p => w.picked.push((p as { x: unknown }).x));\n   255\t        });\n   256\t        const xs = ((await shapes(page, '#chart', type === 'bar' ? 100000 : 14))[1] ?? []).map(s => center(s.box).x).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n   257\t        const labels = type === 'bar' ? SHIPPED.quarters : ENERGY.days.map(calendar);\n   258\t        await page.mouse.move(xs[2]!, (await box(page, '#chart .axylo-proxy')).y + 20);\n   259\t        await settle(page);\n   260\t        const t = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-tooltip');\n   413\t  }\n   414\t\n   415\t  /** Bars that fill the plot's height (author domain [0, 100]), so a tooltip cannot go above or below and is placed beside. */\n   416\t  async function besideBars(page: Page): Promise<{ centres: number[]; tip: Box; plot: Box }> {\n   417\t    await createRaw(page, 'bar', { title: 'Tall', data: ['Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4', 'Q5', 'Q6'].map(q => ({ q, v: 100 })), x: 'q', y: { field: 'v', domain: [0, 100] } });\n   418\t    const centres = ((await shapes(page, '#chart', 100000))[1] ?? []).map(s => center(s.box).x).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n   419\t    const plot = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-proxy');\n   420\t    await page.mouse.move(centres[2]!, plot.y + plot.height / 2);\n   421\t    await settle(page);\n   422\t    const tip = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-tooltip');\n   423\t    return { centres, tip, plot };\n   424\t  }\n   425\t  const title = async (page: Page) => ((await tooltip(page).isVisible()) ? ((await page.locator('#chart .axylo-tooltip .axylo-tooltip-title').textContent()) ?? '') : '');\n   426\t\n   427\t  it('I1 bar: rule 3b converse: without a rest, the straight path to a tooltip placed beside a full-height bar changes the datum as soon as it crosses into the next band', async () => {\n   428\t    const page = await devPage();\n   429\t    const { centres, tip, plot } = await besideBars(page);\n   430\t    // Precondition: the tooltip is beside the bar (not above or below), so the path to it crosses bands.\n   431\t    expect(tip.x > centres[2]! || tip.x + tip.width < centres[2]!, `tooltip ${JSON.stringify(tip)} beside the bar at ${centres[2]}`).toBe(true);\n   432\t    const y = plot.y + plot.height / 2;\n   433\t    const toward = tip.x > centres[2]! ? 1 : -1;\n   434\t    const next = centres[2 + toward]!;\n   435\t    // No rest: arrive and leave at once, in steps of 6 px, past the half-way line to the next band.\n   436\t    await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n   437\t    await page.mouse.move(centres[2]!, y);\n   438\t    const seen: string[] = [];\n   439\t    for (let x = centres[2]!; toward > 0 ? x <= next : x >= next; x += 6 * toward) {\n   440\t      await page.mouse.move(x, y, { steps: 1 });\n   441\t      seen.push(await title(page));\n   442\t    }\n   443\t    await settle(page);\n   444\t    seen.push(await title(page));\n   445\t    expect(seen.at(-1), `datum after crossing: ${seen.join(' → ')}`).toBe(toward > 0 ? 'Q4' : 'Q2');\n   446\t    expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n   447\t  });\n   448\t\n   449\t  it('I1 bar: rule 3b converse: after a rest, leaving the corridor to the tooltip sideways resumes picking on that move', async () => {\n   450\t    const page = await devPage();\n   451\t    const { centres, tip, plot } = await besideBars(page);\n   452\t    const y = plot.y + plot.height / 2;\n   453\t    await page.waitForTimeout(300);\n   454\t    // Part of the way along the corridor (held), then straight up out of it, over the next band.\n   455\t    const toward = tip.x > centres[2]! ? 1 : -1;\n   456\t    const next = centres[2 + toward]!;\n   457\t    await page.mouse.move(next, y, { steps: 6 });\n   458\t    await settle(page);\n   459\t    expect(await title(page), 'held along the corridor').toBe('Q3');\n   460\t    await page.mouse.move(next, Math.max(plot.y + 4, tip.y - 30), { steps: 1 });\n   461\t    await settle(page);\n   462\t    expect(await title(page), 'out of the corridor: the band under the pointer').toBe(toward > 0 ? 'Q4' : 'Q2');\n   463\t    expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n   464\t  });\n   465\t\n   466\t  it('I1 bar: a fast sweep that never rests is never held: one move per band, across a tooltip placed beside the bars, shows every band in turn', async () => {\n   467\t    const page = await devPage();\n   468\t    const { centres, plot } = await besideBars(page);\n   469\t    const y = plot.y + plot.height / 2;\n   470\t    await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n   471\t    const shown: string[] = [];\n   472\t    for (const x of centres) { await page.mouse.move(x, y, { steps: 1 }); await settle(page); shown.push(await title(page)); }\n   473\t    expect(shown).toEqual(['Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4', 'Q5', 'Q6']);\n   474\t    expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n   475\t  });\n   476\t\n   477\t  it('I1 donut: a fast sweep that never rests is never held: one move per slice, around the ring, shows every slice in turn', async () => {\n   478\t    const page = await devPage();\n   479\t    await create(page, 'donut');\n   480\t    const g = await ring(page);\n   481\t    await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n   482\t    const shown: string[] = [];\n   483\t    let before = 0;\n   484\t    for (let i = 0; i < SPEND.values.length; i++) {\n   485\t      const a = (2 * Math.PI * (before + SPEND.values[i]! / 2)) / SPEND_TOTAL;\n   486\t      before += SPEND.values[i]!;\n   487\t      await page.mouse.move(g.cx + 0.85 * g.outer * Math.sin(a), g.cy - 0.85 * g.outer * Math.cos(a), { steps: 1 });\n   718\t      const page = await devPage();\n   719\t      await create(page, type);\n   720\t      const small: string[] = [];\n   721\t      const measure = async (sel: string) => {\n   722\t        for (const el of await page.locator(sel).all()) {\n   723\t          if (!(await el.isVisible())) continue;\n   724\t          const b = (await el.boundingBox())!;\n   725\t          if (b.width < 24 || b.height < 24) small.push(`${(await el.textContent()) || (await el.getAttribute('class'))}: ${b.width.toFixed(1)}×${b.height.toFixed(1)}`);\n   726\t        }\n   727\t      };\n   728\t      // Hovered rows are text (decision 0004 revision 2); pinned rows are buttons, and so are the readout strip's\n   729\t      // entries for a pinned datum: those are measured.\n   730\t      const p = (await probes(page, type))[type === 'donut' ? 2 : 10]!;\n   731\t      await page.mouse.move(p.x, p.y);\n   732\t      await settle(page);\n   733\t      await page.mouse.down();\n   734\t      await page.mouse.up();\n   735\t      await settle(page);\n   736\t      expect(await page.locator('#chart .axylo-tooltip button, #chart .axylo-tooltip [role=\"button\"]').count(), 'pinned rows are buttons').toBeGreaterThan(0);\n   737\t      await measure('#chart .axylo-tooltip button, #chart .axylo-tooltip [role=\"button\"]');\n   738\t      await page.keyboard.press('Escape');\n   739\t      await settle(page);\n   740\t      // Readout mode (plot narrower than 240 px): the strip's entries for a pinned datum.\n   741\t      await plotTo(page, 'width', 200);\n   742\t      const q = (await probes(page, type))[type === 'donut' ? 2 : 4]!;\n   743\t      await page.mouse.move(q.x, q.y);\n   744\t      await page.mouse.down();\n   745\t      await page.mouse.up();\n   746\t      await settle(page);\n   747\t      expect(await page.locator('#chart .axylo-readout button, #chart .axylo-readout [role=\"button\"]').count(), 'pinned strip entries are buttons').toBeGreaterThan(0);\n   748\t      await measure('#chart .axylo-readout button, #chart .axylo-readout [role=\"button\"]');\n   749\t      await page.keyboard.press('Escape');\n   750\t      await page.evaluate(() => { (document.querySelector('#chart') as HTMLElement).style.width = ''; });\n   751\t      await settle(page);\n   752\t      await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n   753\t      // Streaming, so the Pause control is there too.\n   754\t      await call(page, 'append', [more(type, 0)]);\n   755\t      await measure('#chart button, #chart input:not(.a