{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 6 'select:|select\\\\(ref|function pointFor|function emitPoint|function eventPoint' packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts && cat packages/axylo/src/lookup/index.ts | tail -70 && rg -n 'readout|plotKind|ready' packages/axylo/test/core/host.ts | head -38 && rg -n 'RING|surround|Both' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/palette-b.review.md | head -2 | cut -c1-430\"","aggregated_output":"128-\n129-/** What the interaction layer may ask for; everything goes through the public paths. */\n130-export interface ControllerActions {\n131-  zoom(window: Span | null): void;\n132-  toggle(seriesKey: string): void;\n133-  pause(paused: boolean): void;\n134:  select(ref: DatumRef): void;\n135-  hover(ref: DatumRef | null): void;\n136-}\n137-\n138-export interface Controller {\n139-  readonly handle: ChartHandle;\n140-  readonly actions: ControllerActions;\n--\n1444-    }\n1445-  }\n1446-\n1447-  // ── events ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1448-\n1449-  /** The public description of a datum, for `hover` and `select`, from the displayed revision. */\n1450:  function pointFor(d: Drawn, ref: DatumRef): Point<unknown> | null {\n1451-    const text = d.lookup.datum(ref);\n1452-    if (!text) return null;\n1453-    const frame = d.accepted.frame;\n1454-    let x: XValue = 0;\n1455-    let y: number | null = null;\n1456-    if (ref.kind === 'aligned' && frame.shape === 'aligned') {\n--\n1500-      const a = accepted;\n1501-      if (!a || destroyed) return;\n1502-      zoom(window === null ? null : [positionValue(a.frame, window[0]), positionValue(a.frame, window[1])]);\n1503-    },\n1504-    toggle: key => toggleSeries(key),\n1505-    pause: next => setPaused(next),\n1506:    select(ref) {\n1507-      const d = drawn;\n1508-      const point = d && !destroyed ? pointFor(d, ref) : null;\n1509-      if (point) emit('select', point);\n1510-    },\n1511-    hover(ref) {\n1512-      const d = drawn;\nimport type { AlignedView, DonutView, Formatters, Layout, Lookup, ScatterView, View } from '../core/contracts';\nimport type { Messages } from '../public';\nimport { alignedLookup } from './aligned';\nimport { donutLookup } from './donut';\nimport { scatterLookup } from './scatter';\n\n/** A chart kind's lookup, in buildLookup's terms (a kind's composition holds only its own). */\nexport type LookupBuilder = (\n  view: View, layout: Layout, formatters: Formatters, messages: Messages, locale?: string, devicePixelRatio?: number,\n) => Lookup;\n\nfunction plotOf(layout: Layout) {\n  return layout.kind === 'plot' || layout.kind === 'compact' ? layout : null;\n}\n\nexport const donutLookupFor: LookupBuilder = (view, layout, formatters, _messages, locale) =>\n  donutLookup(view as DonutView, plotOf(layout), formatters, locale);\n\nexport const scatterLookupFor: LookupBuilder = (view, layout, formatters, _messages, _locale, devicePixelRatio = 1) =>\n  scatterLookup(view as ScatterView, plotOf(layout), formatters, undefined, devicePixelRatio);\n\nexport const alignedLookupFor: LookupBuilder = (view, layout, formatters, messages) =>\n  alignedLookup(view as AlignedView, plotOf(layout), formatters, messages);\n\n/** The optional locale is retained for callers that supplied it before Formatters owned all readouts. */\nexport function buildLookup(\n  view: View, layout: Layout, formatters: Formatters, messages: Messages, locale?: string, devicePixelRatio = 1,\n): Lookup {\n  switch (view.kind) {\n    case 'donut': return donutLookupFor(view, layout, formatters, messages, locale, devicePixelRatio);\n    case 'scatter': return scatterLookupFor(view, layout, formatters, messages, locale, devicePixelRatio);\n    default: return alignedLookupFor(view, layout, formatters, messages, locale, devicePixelRatio);\n  }\n}\n7:1. **M · The decision extends the surround’s 3:1 result to marks for which it is false. Ran contrast on the opaque colours and the recorded Chrome fill pixels, and inspected both ring implementations.** The focus ink against its background surround is **5.8872:1** in light and **14.4329:1** in dark. The surround passes against all 16 opaque series colours. But all **16 of 16** isolated 25% fills and **6 of 16** isolated 80% \n111:The contrast column also gives the **background-coloured surround against each opaque mark**. Neighbours are other slot numbers in the same scheme. The worst distance is the analytic minimum over all four visions. P, D and T denote protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. Token distances are in focus / reference / muted order.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
