{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'focus|same pixels|two-tone|contrast' docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md | sed -n '/162:/,/175:/p' | cut -c1-225 && rg -n 'zoom|state' packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts | tail -15 && nl -ba packages/axylo/src/dom/pointer.ts | head -22 && rg -n 'interaction:' packages/axylo/src/kinds/*.ts && git ls-tree -r --name-only a518cbb -- apps/docs | rg -i 'conformance|wcag'\"","aggregated_output":"162:The second review (part B, finding 1) showed that a single-ink focus indicator cannot work with these colors:\n166:A datum outline crossing a mark therefore fails WCAG 1.4.11 wherever it is drawn in one ink. The chart core is changing the indicator to two tones: a ring in the focus token, with a surround in the background color betwee\n168:**What the token must satisfy under the two-tone ring:**\n170:1. **The focus color must reach 3:1 against the background.** The ring is seen against its surround, which is the background color. Light `#1f5fcc` on `#ffffff` is 5.89:1; dark `#e3e8f0` on `#16181d` is 14.43:1. Both pass\n172:3. **The focus color needs no contrast against series colors.** The surround keeps them from touching.\n174:**Constraint 5 is no longer needed for contrast.** That constraint is the 0.10 OKLab distance between every series color and the focus token, and it never could provide contrast: an OKLab distance is not a contrast ratio.\n210:| Lowest contrast, light / dark | 3.03 / 3.26 | 3.03 / 3.09 | 3.10 / 3.07 |\n218:- **Tighter dark margins to the tokens:** focus 0.104 and muted 0.102. The superseded set had 0.138 and 0.113.\n240:Weighted p10 / median contrast, by renderer and device pixel ratio (`strokes.json`):\n284:- **Lowest contrast:** 3.03 light (slate), 3.26 dark (purple).\n296:3. **Dark against that light set.** The searches with the old focus token failed: `dark-a2.json` (annealing) and `dark-n2.json` (exact; best blue L 0.55). Moving the dark focus to near-white let annealing find a set with \n326:- **Magenta fourth instead of purple**, to relieve the dark blue (`configs/mag4-a.json`): feasible on white. Its dark set was proved infeasible with the old focus token (exact search, `configs/dark-n2-m4.json`), and annea\n343:- **The dark focus ring is near-white `#e3e8f0`** (light stays blue).\n345:  - With the two-tone ring it meets its contrast need (14.4:1 on the background).\n346:  - Reverting to `#79a8ff` is possible under two tones only if constraint 5 is dropped: it is 0.050 from the dark blue (see \"Focus token under a two-tone ring\").\n379:  - `keyboard.browser.test.ts` checks the light focus only, and that token is unchanged.\n382:- **The focus ring.** The two-tone focus ring is being built in the chart core. Its rendered contrast against marks has not been measured here.\n66:        report[state] = violations.map(v => `${v.id}: ${v.help} (${v.nodes.join(', ')})`);\n69:        if (state === 'table open' && fixture === 'trend') expect(ran).toContain('scrollable-region-focusable');\n72:      // Which states apply follows from the fixture (spec C1, L7, 3.6).\n82:describe('axe-core in the states the fixture loop does not reach (review 2, finding 21)', () => {\n83:  it('trend paused, zoomed, in the narrow readout and in the internal-error state: no violations; undecided rules listed apart', async () => {\n88:    const check = async (state: string) => {\n90:      results[state] = { violations: violations.map(v => v.id), incomplete };\n91:      expect(ran, state).toContain('heading-order');\n99:    await check('zoomed');\n113:    for (const [state, r] of Object.entries(results)) expect(r.violations, state).toEqual([]);\n135:    expect(controls.map(c => c.text)).toEqual(['Direct', 'Organic search', 'Referral', 'Zoom in', 'Zoom out', 'Pan left', 'Pan right', 'Reset zoom', 'Pause', 'View as table']);\n174:    await make(page, 'trend', { messages: { zoomIn: 'Vergrößern' } });\n180:        zoomIn: button('Vergrößern')?.getAttribute('lang') ?? null, zoomInEffective: lang(button('Vergrößern')),\n181:        zoomOut: button('Zoom out')?.getAttribute('lang') ?? null,\n186:    expect(langs).toEqual({ toolbar: 'en', zoomIn: 'de', zoomInEffective: 'de', zoomOut: 'en', table: 'en', legend: 'de' });\n     1\t/**\n     2\t * Comparing pick targets. Pointer, touch and drag input are handled by the interaction layer\n     3\t * (dom/interaction.ts); this only says whether two targets name the same thing.\n     4\t */\n     5\timport type { PickTarget } from '../core/contracts';\n     6\t\n     7\t/** Two pick results name the same thing, so the tooltip need not be rebuilt. */\n     8\texport function sameTarget(a: PickTarget | null, b: PickTarget | null): boolean {\n     9\t  if (a === null || b === null) return a === b;\n    10\t  if (a.kind === 'x' && b.kind === 'x') return a.x === b.x;\n    11\t  if (a.kind === 'slice' && b.kind === 'slice') return a.sliceKey === b.sliceKey;\n    12\t  if (a.kind === 'point' && b.kind === 'point') {\n    13\t    return a.count === b.count && a.refs.length === b.refs.length && a.refs.every((r, i) => {\n    14\t      const o = b.refs[i]!;\n    15\t      return r.kind === 'point' && o.kind === 'point' && r.seriesKey === o.seriesKey && r.row === o.row && r.x === o.x;\n    16\t    });\n    17\t  }\n    18\t  return false;\n    19\t}\npackages/axylo/src/kinds/scatter.ts:22:  interaction: { overlay: scatterTargetMarks, swatch: pointSwatch, stepInSeries, sliceList: null },\npackages/axylo/src/kinds/donut.ts:22:  interaction: { overlay: donutTargetMarks, swatch: pointSwatch, stepInSeries: null, sliceList: donutSliceList },\npackages/axylo/src/kinds/bar.ts:22:  interaction: { overlay: alignedTargetMarks, swatch: barSwatch, stepInSeries: null, sliceList: null },\npackages/axylo/src/kinds/area.ts:22:  interaction: { overlay: alignedTargetMarks, swatch: areaSwatch, stepInSeries: null, sliceList: null },\npackages/axylo/src/kinds/line.ts:22:  interaction: { overlay: alignedTargetMarks, swatch: lineSwatch, stepInSeries: null, sliceList: null },\napps/docs/pages/conformance.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
